div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1407841#post1407841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You win. Can you just ban me from the site if only certain opinions are allowed now.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Take a few days off.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T03:19:16-07:00","id":1407884,"title":"","content":"If I were to combine tribes, there are few I'd make two in a heartbeat.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers+Bone Gnawers- Glass Walkers is a great tribe written VERY well in revised, Bone Gnawers have great books but,well. As I've grown older, the concept of the Bone Gnawers has become far less tolerable. It isn't that garou cannot live in the slums, but the mentality of why and why that makes them lesser. The idea that the status among garou reflects status among humans is not only rather weird (since most tribes are made out of moochers to the kinfolk) but also has edges of 'well, they are poor because SPIRITUALLY they are destined to be poor.' Combination of these two could easily allow city-garou to swing from homeless theurges mumbling to ahroun trained by their military kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Black Furies/Stargazers/Bone Gnawers+Children of Gaia- This is mostly because CoG just cannot get a break in writing. Every other tribebook has been at least usable, but CoG revised is worth its scorn. Combining them with Furies might give them a chance to be a decent camp.<br /> <br /> As for the Stargazer combo, Stargazers fit in the same bracket of 'human-philosophy tribe' and they are generally seen as annoying as Coggies. Being a more global tribe might help their image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T04:54:23-07:00","id":1407892,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar479_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"479\" data-vbnamecard=\"479\">Damian May</a> awesome! I\u2019ve read a couple things for Forsaken, but I\u2019m not as familiar with it as I am with Apocalypse. The Great Wolf story sounds like a great way to combine the two games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T04:55:48-07:00","id":1407893,"title":"","content":"The extend that I'd mess with the Tribes depends a lot on what the design goal would be. Given that we're talking about W5, I'd keep all 13 Tribes, and focus on retooling them to address various issues. Saying that the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers have always been the same Tribe as a retcon don't sit that well with me, and I can't imagine a metaplot event that would ever really justify it. I could see some reshuffling or changes around the Stargazers (simply for how small they are) and the Children of Gaia (for how ineffective they've been) where you can at least come up with reasons they've ceased to exist as independent Tribes.<br /> <br /> If I didn't feel like there needed to be some level of reasonably continuity with pre-W5, there's a lot more I would change in a few ares.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T05:40:41-07:00","id":1407903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1407884#post1407884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to combine tribes, there are few I'd make two in a heartbeat.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers+Bone Gnawers- Glass Walkers is a great tribe written VERY well in revised, Bone Gnawers have great books but,well. As I've grown older, the concept of the Bone Gnawers has become far less tolerable. It isn't that garou cannot live in the slums, but the mentality of why and why that makes them lesser. The idea that the status among garou reflects status among humans is not only rather weird (since most tribes are made out of moochers to the kinfolk) but also has edges of 'well, they are poor because SPIRITUALLY they are destined to be poor.' Combination of these two could easily allow city-garou to swing from homeless theurges mumbling to ahroun trained by their military kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Black Furies/Stargazers/Bone Gnawers+Children of Gaia- This is mostly because CoG just cannot get a break in writing. Every other tribebook has been at least usable, but CoG revised is worth its scorn. Combining them with Furies might give them a chance to be a decent camp.<br /> <br /> As for the Stargazer combo, Stargazers fit in the same bracket of 'human-philosophy tribe' and they are generally seen as annoying as Coggies. Being a more global tribe might help their image.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel conflicted, I love the Bone Gnawers because their dirty furry Antifa. Through I do know that the Bone Gnawers thing of people that chose to be poor, because their lazy, and it\u2019s it\u2019s their genes to be poor, has a similar to poor shaming shit,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T06:12:14-07:00","id":1407913,"title":"","content":"-The Fianna need to stop being so Irish. I've said it before, but their archtype is pretty common across the world and they would do well emphasizing sub-tribes. I like the celtic origins, I really dig the stag symbolism and the &quot;We fight to boast so we can fuck&quot; lad culture that it represents, but it can't be an irish-american caricature anymore.<br /> <br /> -Wendigo:<br /> You've got to shift the 'fuck white people' stance to 'fuck modernity and fuck the european tribes that rode in on it' whilst also balancing ideas of racial purity and superiority. That might confuse a few of you (Isn't he saying to do the same thing?) but it's not; The wendigo, as a tribe, don't hate all white people, because most white people aren't responsible for manifest destiny. They hate the leaders of the white people, and they hate the businessmen of the white people who rape the land; and they resent the Garou who stole their caerns, failed to check modernity in their own lands, and brought their failure with them to the new world. The Wendigo could be an interesting balancing game concerning modernity and kinfolk; On one hand, technology is evil and like all garou they long for the times it wasn't there. On the otherhand, their kinfolk <i>want</i> modernity; they want convenience, they want modern structures, cars, phones; and the booze too. Booze aside, wouldn't they be sabotaging their own people if they pushed for the exclusion of modernity?<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, given past performance, I can't imagine W5 capturing nuance with the wendigo.<br /> <br /> Black Furies<br /> No Trans-homids, don't even try it. Pegasus cares for Sex, not your gender identity; he's bitter that someone mutilated his genitals: he's not going to take you if you willingly go through the op. I like my mostly TERF furies, thank you. The Children of Gaia have what you're looking for. The Furies are good the way they are.<br /> <br /> Stargazers:<br /> I think the intention is that they're supposed to repulse us. The important thing is that we don't make them <i>the</i> asian werewolves, we make them <i>a</i> tribe of asian werewolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tribes in general: <br /> I think there's a happy place between 1/2nd era where the tribes are dysfunctional and revised/V20 era where things are way more optimistic and the tribes can all get along and reasonably beat the wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T07:53:31-07:00","id":1407937,"title":"","content":"There is a balancing act between making the tribes too dysfunctional, and making them too perfect. But I think it's possible to give them flaws and serious problems without making it ridiculous (Children of Gaia) or a pile of derogatory stereotypes (Younger Brother).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1407884#post1407884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Furies/Stargazers/Bone Gnawers+Children of Gaia- This is mostly because CoG just cannot get a break in writing. Every other tribebook has been at least usable, but CoG revised is worth its scorn. Combining them with Furies might give them a chance to be a decent camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really can't agree on the Black Furies. They are very distinct in their purpose as avengers.<br /> <br /> And like Heavy Arms, I want to avoid drastic retcons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  got two tribes confused, oops 08-13-2020, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T09:44:15-07:00","id":1407966,"title":"","content":"IMO CoG are the worst tribe because they want to reject tribalism (They're the best tribe in terms of gifts) and tribalism's what WTA's about. <br /> The best way of having them fit in is by making them hypocritically tribal. IE they're the superior beings for not being judgemental; &quot;We'll give the minority a voice even if we have to shout out the majority; you best accept peace or we'll kill you all.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> The horrid stuff in the tribebooks is a gross overreaction that doesn't really speak to anything on an adult level. Tribes should poke at something that feels 'real' not something that one person with an extreme view has imagined. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:42:52-07:00","id":1407982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1407913#post1407913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The Fianna need to stop being so Irish. I've said it before, but their archtype is pretty common across the world and they would do well emphasizing sub-tribes. I like the celtic origins, I really dig the stag symbolism and the &amp;quot;We fight to boast so we can fuck&amp;quot; lad culture that it represents, but it can't be an irish-american caricature anymore.<br /> <br /> -Wendigo:<br /> You've got to shift the 'fuck white people' stance to 'fuck modernity and fuck the european tribes that rode in on it' whilst also balancing ideas of racial purity and superiority. That might confuse a few of you (Isn't he saying to do the same thing?) but it's not; The wendigo, as a tribe, don't hate all white people, because most white people aren't responsible for manifest destiny. They hate the leaders of the white people, and they hate the businessmen of the white people who rape the land; and they resent the Garou who stole their caerns, failed to check modernity in their own lands, and brought their failure with them to the new world. The Wendigo could be an interesting balancing game concerning modernity and kinfolk; On one hand, technology is evil and like all garou they long for the times it wasn't there. On the otherhand, their kinfolk <i>want</i> modernity; they want convenience, they want modern structures, cars, phones; and the booze too. Booze aside, wouldn't they be sabotaging their own people if they pushed for the exclusion of modernity?<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, given past performance, I can't imagine W5 capturing nuance with the wendigo.<br /> <br /> Black Furies<br /> No Trans-homids, don't even try it. Pegasus cares for Sex, not your gender identity; he's bitter that someone mutilated his genitals: he's not going to take you if you willingly go through the op. I like my mostly TERF furies, thank you. The Children of Gaia have what you're looking for. The Furies are good the way they are.<br /> <br /> Stargazers:<br /> I think the intention is that they're supposed to repulse us. The important thing is that we don't make them <i>the</i> asian werewolves, we make them <i>a</i> tribe of asian werewolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tribes in general: <br /> I think there's a happy place between 1/2nd era where the tribes are dysfunctional and revised/V20 era where things are way more optimistic and the tribes can all get along and reasonably beat the wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that the Wendigo probably hate the leaders of the white people more than they hate all white people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T11:49:48-07:00","id":1407995,"title":"","content":"To some of your points on tribes MyWifeIsScary - baring in mind that this is simply my opinion on the matter - although many of these could very well be entire threads on their own and may well have been in the past:<br /> <br /> \u2022Fianna<br /> -We\u2019ve definitely discussed this before and while I agree that more can be done to distinguish them from Irish stereotypes, I feel that their expanded lore via revised tribe books has done that well. Their name is derived from their history and I personally don\u2019t see any reason to extract them from their Gaelic-Celtic roots so long as tribes with ethnic ties remain part of the game.<br /> <br /> \u2022Younger Brother<br /> -I disagree with your characterization of Younger Brother - while all tribes do certainly reject modernity, barring the Glass Walkers primarily - I would consider it a gross disservice to makes Younger Brother the tribe of technological rejection - a task the Red Talons already have chosen. Indigenous groups have embraced western technology quite well, with the goal of adaption and survivance, and before colonization many indigenous groups practiced highly refined land maintenance and scientific-technological traditions. I feel it would be more accurate to describe Younger Brother as particularly tradition minded - a vanguard of language, land, and ceremony. I also feel that extracting Younger Brother from a justified anger towards colonial populations does the tribe a disservice. I agree that Younger Brother should not be portrayed as constantly \u201ckill whitey\u201d and that the leaders who bring about colonial infrastructure should be central enemies, the point remains that Younger Brother has a justified anger over an apocalyptic loss of culture and life and while today there is certainly no easy answer to the vast populations of non-indigenous folk in North America, Younger Brother (and players identifying with him) should be allowed the catharsis of resentment.<br /> <br /> \u2022Black Furies<br /> -I adamantly disagree with your representation of the Black Furies. The history of transgender people throughout numerous societies and spiritual traditions aside, a game defined by its punk nature should not be creating barriers against real world trans people. I feel that trans woman should be accepted by the Black Furies, or at least, by Pegasus. I do agree that the tribe should certainly retain camps that maintain a TERF attitude, but interaction with such elements should be optional in play - if a trans woman wants to play someone like herself in WtA through the Black Furies and doesn\u2019t want to deal with harassment she already endured in her real life, that should not only be possible but encouraged and celebrated.<br /> <br /> \u2022Stargazers<br /> -While I certainly agree that they should be \u2018a\u2019 tribe of Asian werewolves as opposed to \u2018the\u2019 tribe of Asian werewolves, I don\u2019t understand what you mean by \u201cthey\u2019re meant to repulse us\u201d.<br /> <br /> \u2022Children of Gaia<br /> -I do agree that their tribe book is just, ugh, varying from lackluster to annoying to just gross at various times. That said, I do also agree that the negative side of the Children of Gaia should be shown through their attempts to mediate conflicts without truly understanding the anger of either side as well as they arrogance, hypocrisy, desire for \u2018purity\u2019 under Unicorn, and their belief that only they can truly unite the Garou Nation. I also believe that they should be celebrated though for their willingness to pursue peace in a culture of war, their willingness to accept anyone, their truly idealistic ambition, their fierce willingness to defend innocent and purity, and their drive to unite the Garou with humanity - even if it leaves them exposed.<br /> <br /> The Children of Gaia have been shortchanged for a long time in my opinion, when they have the potential to be as inspiring and interesting through their virtues and flaws as any tribe.<br /> <br /> \u2022Tribes<br /> -I do agree that their should be a happy medium between the dysfunction of 1st/2nd edition and the sometimes overly-strident revision of revised tradition. Each tribe should be flawed and problematic, each should have flaws of the past and present, that define where they are today and why they are potentially a threat to Balance. They should also be celebrated though, each tribe unique and highly qualified in certain areas, leaps and bounds ahead of others, qualities of their Rage and Character which can inspire us to join their fight and see how their vision might just avert the Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T13:14:22-07:00","id":1408008,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2022Stargazers</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">-While I certainly agree that they should be \u2018a\u2019 tribe of Asian werewolves as opposed to \u2018the\u2019 tribe of Asian werewolves, I don\u2019t understand what you mean by \u201cthey\u2019re meant to repulse us\u201d.[/quote]</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They're not very werewolf like, are they. They're &quot;different&quot; and that's deliberate; Stargazers and their strange, rage denying ways are meant to make other garou feel uncomfortable. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022Younger Brother<br /> -I disagree with your characterization of Younger Brother </div> </div> </div>You don't really, looks more like a communication failure. We're mostly on the same page. I think a good chunk of Wendigo should hold great resentment for all whites, and a great many have ideas about the superiority of indigenous races: The European Garou fucked up in Europe, and the American Garou were doing fine till the europeans came.. That's a testament to which tribe is better. But I also think a good chunck recognize that modern first nations people aren't that different from europeans, and try to place their anger on the right europeans. I don't think the tribe should become anti-modernity like the talons, it's more that they're in an interesting possition where much of modernity is newer to their people and they have more agency in effecting that than european tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022Black Furies<br /> -I adamantly disagree with your representation of the Black Furies. The history of transgender people throughout numerous societies and spiritual traditions aside, a game defined by its punk nature should not be creating barriers against real world trans people. </div> </div> </div>Most trans people I've played with don't play trans people, they play the sex they want to be. And if they do want to play trans people, it's likely because they want to fight for their rights in game. A game defined by it's punk nature should thus have an enemy for trans people to fight with, and the furies fit the bill as a potentially hot battleground. You're of course welcome to play a trans metis in the black furies, and I think the black furies would indeed attract many trans metis who want to be women black furies. The Metis are a very interesting metaphor for players who want to struggle with their condition whatever it is. Again: Trans players almost always play cis characters of their desired sex. If trans players want it easy, they have that option, and if trans players want the glorious struggle, they have the option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022Children of Gaia<br /> I also believe that they should be celebrated though for their willingness to pursue peace in a culture of war, their willingness to accept anyone, their truly idealistic ambition, their fierce willingness to defend innocent and purity, and their drive to unite the Garou with humanity </div> </div> </div>These are all reasons to shit on them, honestly; You can't have a decisive war if half your soldiers are looking for compromise, you lose social cohesion by accepting anyone, a truly idealistic ambition is for fools who fuck up big time, Innocence and purity is a trap, and humanity is the enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T13:57:45-07:00","id":1408017,"title":"","content":"\u2022Stargazers<br /> -Ah, gotcha, I think I see what you\u2019re trying to say. I don\u2019t entirely agree that \u2018repulsive\u2019 is the right term, but I can understand making them seem strange from the perspective of western Garou, particularly by putting focus on the Stargazer\u2019s struggle to overcome rage - which they view as they great undermining of the Garou.<br /> <br /> \u2022Younger Brother<br /> -Put that way, I do think I agree with you more. One of Younger Brother\u2019s issues imo is how he pushes away Older Brother for what he perceives as \u2018surrender\u2019 and \u2018abandoning himself\u2019. Younger Brother\u2019s tribe love their kinfolk boundlessly, but I can definitely see them being displeased by any who would seek to live outside the community and live as the colonizers do.<br /> <br /> \u2022Black Furies<br /> -This looks like it\u2019s going to be one of the places where you and I are generally going to disagree. I can certainly see a trans woman choosing to play a cis woman, but I also think it\u2019s just as possible that she would choose to play a trans woman. I also agree that the fight against tribal attitudes may well be very useful and cathartic, but that story should be one that is opted into through use of groups/camps of Black Furies in my opinion, as opposed to being the default status of the tribe. I also wouldn\u2019t say it\u2019s about having it easy - it\u2019s about not wanting to deal with one\u2019s constant real life problems in one\u2019s RPG hobby fun time. I\u2019m also not entirely sure what the purpose of bringing the garou-born into this is.<br /> <br /> \u2022Children of Gaia<br /> -This seems to be a place where you and I simply disagree. Where, in the end, has constant war gotten the Garou Nation? If peace is possible in a situation that conflict can be avoided and lives saved, that should be celebrated. The Garou Nation is too few to die frivolously and life is too important. The Children of Gaia fight when they must, only the misguided or saintly won\u2019t. Is social cohesion important enough to abandon someone? The Children accept anyone seeking them into their tribe, they accommodate their beliefs and teach them their customs and ideals. The Children of Gaia are a tribe of all Gaia\u2019s children who seek them out and willingly take up Unicorn\u2019s cause. That found community can create just as strong a bond, if not a stronger one in some, then community by blood. Ideals are what we strive to achieve, the Garou who have truly abandoned their ideals are those walking with death wishes, nearing harano, gone Ronin, or Dancing the Spiral. One can\u2019t live the life that the Garou do without some sort of ideals, no matter how cynical they may become. Innocence and Purity do exist, Unicorn knows that and protects them wherever found because it\u2019s inherently worthy of protection. There are places that darkness has not touched, thoughts that are warm, people that are good, those who like children and animals - are innocent. Those are Unicorn\u2019s protectorate and what the Children of Gaia would happily die with bloodied claws to protect. Humanity is just a common name for a bunch of humans; some good, some bad, most just decent and getting by. They have altered the world and only they have the power to alter it again. They are one half of the Garou - they cannot be discounted, just as wolves cannot be discounted. Humans too are Gaia\u2019s children.<br /> <br /> More then any other tribe, the Children of Gaia place their hopes upon humanity and call them kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T14:31:02-07:00","id":1408027,"title":"","content":"If Pegasus cared so much about sex or gender essentialism, the inclusion of cis-male Black Furies with penises in the Tribe wouldn't really make sense; whatever mental gymnastics to only allow Metis cis-male Black Furies into the Tribe.<br /> <br /> Pegasus don't need to be a TERF for there to be TERF Furies (who are more likely to be Elders and so on) to have as internal enemies for trans Furies and their allies to fight against.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:08:23-07:00","id":1408038,"title":"","content":"Why the heck are you going on a random, off-topic political rant about the Vietnam war? It has nothing to do with this conversation. I know that the WoD involves real world politics, but please do not turn this thread into your personal soapbox for your unrelated political projects. Especially if you don't bother to use actual facts.<br /> <br /> The Children of Gaia are not, or should never be depicted as, people who want peace with the Wyrm. They want peace between the Gaian Garou tribes, <i>so that they can wage a united war against the Wyrm</i>. I thought this was obvious, even despite whatever garbage was printed in their tribebook(s).<br /> <br /> They also accept mules, nonconformists, and other Garou who all other tribes reject or horribly abuse - especially mules. Consider that the Black Spiral Dancers canonically increase <i>more</i> from recruits than from their own breeding. The Gaian Garou create their own worst enemies with their excessively narrow definitions of who is a worthy werewolf, driving out far too many decent Gaians who then turn to the Black Spiral out of desperation. Only the Children of Gaia and Bone Gnawers truly open their arms as an alternative. The Garou cannot win the war if they keep driving so many of their population straight to the Spiral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-13-2020, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:29:02-07:00","id":1408044,"title":"","content":"Furies are much MUCH more interesting when Pegasus is not stepping in to say which side is right in the trans-debate. Seriously, that is interesting RP stuff I like, when the tribe has no answer and goes by situation to situation.<br /> <br /> As for the CoGies, the flaw I've always liked to give them is that their Elders are too busy to teach their cubs or cliaths and as such the cliath end up like in the CoG revised story. What do you do, when your youth truly cannot comprehend the message and duty? When you and every other ranked garou is too busy with their projects to teach them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:32:40-07:00","id":1408046,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m seconding what Heavy Arms is saying above.<br /> <br /> \u2022Black Furies<br /> -This isn\u2019t about \u2018Need\u2019 imo and if we want to get into some fun fun intersectionality theory then I can make an argument for \u2018need\u2019 but I won\u2019t do that now, what I say is that this isn\u2019t about need imo. I\u2019m glad that a trans woman could play a trans woman in the CoG, Pure Tribes, GW, GG, etcetera; but we aren\u2019t talking about them. We\u2019re talking about the Black Furies and I\u2019m saying that any player, but particularly a trans woman, should be able to play a trans woman within the Black Furies.<br /> <br /> As to the garou-born, I could see an argument being made for dysmorphia to qualify and if a player wanted to explore dysmorphia through the garou-born and I thought they could do it effectively without negatively impacting the game, I would probably allow them to do so. The issue comes from the messaging, as so much does with the garou-born. If the only trans garou are represented by the garou-born who are deemed abominations whose existence is in violation to sacred law - well, in optics speak, that\u2019s a Bad Look\u2122\ufe0f. I\u2019d say that if there were more exploration of trans characters and themes amongst homids, it would be less of a concern, but this very discussion shows that\u2019s not the case. <br /> <br /> If someone wanted to establish in their setting that all Garou who would be born trans are born into the appropriate body instead, thanks to spiritual intervention, and a group just wants to say that to sidestep the issue entirely - fine. However that removes a potentially important discussion from the table, and so I think that unless a table specifically wants to opt for that option, it does a disservice. Trans people should be in just as much a position to explore issues relevant to them through Werewolf as an environmental activist, person of indigenous heritage, or person in poverty might be. That should be the game\u2019s default imo.<br /> <br /> Session 0 is an important tool, I agree, but it is an optional one and one that appears much later in reading a book like Werewolf then the setting chapter, which are in the front and establish the status quo. If a potential players reads the default lore of the Black Furies and discovers them to be a tribe of TERFs and are turned off of them because of that; it does the player, game, and setting a disservice. Every tribe should be flawed, sometimes to the point of dysfunction if the game calls for it, but their default state should not be so flawed that a player could not imagine playing a heroic Garou of righteous fury within that tribe. This is ultimately the reason why I feel that camps of Black Furies with TERF mentalities should exist, but occupy the same role of other antagonistic camps. Manifestations of flaws within the tribe which undoubtably exist but which are combatable from a player\u2019s level and perspective.<br /> <br /> \u2022Children of Gaia<br /> -And plenty of wars and bloodshed could have been avoided if superpowers such as the US and USSR didn\u2019t back parties in conflicts on a different level then their own, creating cycles of repercussion that we see to this very day.<br /> <br /> I see your point and agree - not every gesture towards peace will be a winning strategy in the long term. Yet, sometimes peace making does work. It\u2019s usually impossible to tell without the benefit of hindsight. However, the alternative mindset, that one should choose conflict rather then pursue peace because there\u2019s a chance that things could be worse later is not a superior ideology in my opinion.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation\u2019s history, writ large, is a testament to the repercussion of unnecessary conflict and bloodshed. The Garou have to live in hiding - because they scarred humanity so thoroughly that they have a supernatural terror of the wilderness. The Garou are alone in their fight - because they slaughtered potential allies and throughly embittered most of those they didn\u2019t kill. The Garou tribes are divided - because they\u2019ve been battling over petty shit for centuries and would rather hold grudges then bury the hatchet in Gaia\u2019s name.<br /> <br /> Some conflicts are necessary to ensure a better future and create a better world. No Garou within the Garou Nation would deny that and I think that most people would agree to some level or another. The stance that the Children of Gaia take, which makes them stand distinct from the Nation, is that the only conflicts that should be fought are the ones which are absolutely necessary.<br /> <br /> The Children of Gaia are overcome with shame for their past participation in the Impergium, Wars of Rage, and Wars of Tears. They know that their hands are as dirty as anyone else\u2019s and that it might be too late. But, they haven\u2019t stopped fighting. They\u2019re trying to make amends. Trying to heal old wounds. They\u2019re doing what no other tribe is and what might be one of the most important things any tribe could ever do - they\u2019re trying to break the cycle of violence.<br /> <br /> The Garou are warriors - they all are. This holds true for Younger Brother and the Get of Fenris just as much as it holds true for the Bone Gnawers and the Children of Gaia. The Children of Gaia simply choose their battles differently, but when they believe the cause is righteous and the bloodshed is necessary - they are just as capable of upholding their sacred duty as any other tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:38:29-07:00","id":1408049,"title":"","content":"The whole military history screed also really doesn't make the point it seems to want to.<br /> <br /> To paraphrase my grandfather, who grew up during WWI, became an adult in the aftermath, and fled Europe in the 30s: The worst thing to happen in the 20th Century was that Allies deciding that WWI had to end in an utterly decisive victory that forced a humiliating surrender by the Germans so they'd &quot;never&quot; challenge the Allies again.<br /> <br /> The desire to make the the Central Powers suffer for the war, and the economic and political sanctions the Allies put on them in the peace agreements are directly linked to the rises of Fascism and Communism, as the Allies destroyed the stability of the old governments and made the populaces increasingly open to radical forms of governance to reclaim stability, economic promise, and national pride.<br /> <br /> And that's the exact sort of thing the CoG opposes. Beating your opponents so badly they embrace extremism means losing the war against the Wyrm. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar896_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"896\" data-vbnamecard=\"896\">Erinys</a> <br /> points out, this is literally the case just with Garou being shoved out of the Nation over such mentalities.<br /> <br /> The end of WWI made things worse because it was about beating the enemy into submission. The end of WWII made Europe a far better place (even with the rise of the USSR and the Cold War) thanks to the commitment to the Marshall Plan and recognizing that the point isn't to reenact Rome's salting of Carthage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T20:45:06-07:00","id":1408096,"title":"","content":"I'm not even sure why folks are arguing.<br /> <br /> Its canon that the only TERFs left in the Furies are some crusty elders in one of the smallest camps.<br /> <br /> Pegasus is Trans herself and accepts Transwomen, Intersex and non-binary folks and has for a couple of editions now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T23:48:53-07:00","id":1408108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408096#post1408096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pegasus is Trans herself and accepts Transwomen, Intersex and non-binary folks and has for a couple of editions now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's this written? Ignoring the metis loophole. I haven't found it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T05:19:35-07:00","id":1408129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1407966#post1407966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO CoG are the worst tribe because they want to reject tribalism (They're the best tribe in terms of gifts) and tribalism's what WTA's about. <br /> <br /> The best way of having them fit in is by making them hypocritically tribal. IE they're the superior beings for not being judgemental; &amp;quot;We'll give the minority a voice even if we have to shout out the majority; you best accept peace or we'll kill you all.&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> The horrid stuff in the tribebooks is a gross overreaction that doesn't really speak to anything on an adult level. Tribes should poke at something that feels 'real' not something that one person with an extreme view has imagined. </div> </div> </div> </div>What. I know the revised Tribebook is crap,but I don\u2019t think values of peace and equality, are things only children would believe in,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T05:38:26-07:00","id":1408135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408129#post1408129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What. I know the revised Tribebook is crap,but I don\u2019t think values of peace and equality, are things only children would believe in,</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. Same do the Black Furies, the Glass Walkers and the Bone Gnawers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T06:17:10-07:00","id":1408140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408108#post1408108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's this written? Ignoring the metis loophole. I haven't found it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://keepontheheathlands.com/2016/11/04/trans-representation-changing-face-werewolf/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://keepontheheathlands.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/Werewolf-Banner-1024x576.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://keepontheheathlands.com/2016/11/04/trans-representation-changing-face-werewolf/\" target=\"_blank\"> Trans Representation and the Changing Face of Werewolf - Keep on the Heathlands </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://keepontheheathlands.com/2016/11/04/trans-representation-changing-face-werewolf/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://keepontheheathlands.com/2016/11/04/trans-representation-changing-face-werewolf/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Trans Representation and the Changing Face of Werewolf by Lang Schmitt Early on in the new Werewolf: the Apocalypse BNS book we meet Verity Argyris.&nbsp; Verity is a young Black Fury historian who&rsquo;s working to record the oral histories of the Garou, and her observations are scattered throughout the book. After many pages of meeting &hellip; Continue reading \"Trans Representation and the Changing Face of Werewolf\" </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:11:51-07:00","id":1408159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408140#post1408140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://keepontheheathlands.com/2016/11/04/trans-representation-changing-face-werewolf/\" target=\"_blank\">http://keepontheheathlands.com/2016/...face-werewolf/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>So... No, you can't find it either. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">BNS's MET isn't canon and it should stay that way forever. </span></span></span> The writer here seems rather aware of what the BF's were originally supposed to be (inspired by trans-exclusive wica groups they say?) , but seems to fail to grasp some of the fundamental ideas of the setting; Hyper-toxic masculinity in werewolf isn't a flaw, it's a feature. The game's above all else is about Rage and, no, I don't think Trans people are a Glass Walker exclusive. The writer has a clear bias, but the crux of the issue remains the same; There is no canonical source which allows for any male-sex homid or lupus to join the Black Fury Tribe; That's their thing. <br /> <br /> I strongly suspect the original writers allowed male metis specifically into the black furies to represent Trans inclusion, which comes with a considerable number of Jar-of-worms implications. I feel, artistically, this was a powerful move and is excellent allegory, and I think trans-homid characters should really gravitate towards the 9 of the 13 tribes that wouldn't take issue*. Politically, I recognize some of you might take issue with that. Looking at the changes V5 made, they are not about art, they're about accessibility, so things are likely to swing your way. Probably the more pressing question is if they'll portray the Black Furies accepting Trans homids as an in-universe transition or a total retcon. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Shadow lords, Get of Fenrir, Fianna and Black Furies. Though Female-to-male characters are probably welcomed by these some of these tribes. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:13:32-07:00","id":1408160,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll think the Icehearts and Uktena would be accepting of LGBT people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:24:41-07:00","id":1408164,"title":"","content":"Having NO modern, welcoming Black Furies would be as ridiculous as leaving the game's present-day date in 2003.<br /> <br /> It's 2020. The setting will advance past 2003. There's no sense in pretending it won't or shouldn't.<br /> <br /> If you want ALL werewolves and humans everywhere to keep the hate-filled bigotry of the 18th century, with no exceptions whatsoever, you should just play Werewolf: the Wild West. If the modern world offends you so horribly, you don't have to play in it, or worry about a book set in the modern day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408160#post1408160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll think the Icehearts and Uktena would be accepting of LGBT people.</div> </div> </div> </div>They definitely would. Many native cultures recognize more than two genders. Maybe the same with the Stargazers, although I don't know if Tibetan or central Asian cultures allow equivalents of hijra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-14-2020, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:31:47-07:00","id":1408167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408164#post1408164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having NO modern, welcoming Black Furies would be as ridiculous as leaving the game's present-day date in 2003.<br /> <br /> It's 2020. The setting will advance past 2003. There's no sense in pretending it won't or shouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, while I consider BNS book PRETTY bad, I do think the setting would do well with not having a clearcut answer for the Furies regarding trans-women. Like how the Strider book had them argue about abortions. The tribe being split about it is much more interesting than a clear answer from Pegasus. After all, Stag and Falcon accept metis among their ranks... but their tribes treat them like crap and neither totem has bothered to correct them. Nevermind the Man-Eater from the BF revised book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:42:31-07:00","id":1408171,"title":"","content":"Even in the Revised tribebook, it's an unanswered question how Pegasus would react to a Black Fury who grew a penis and balls due to the Metamorphic Plague. An the Black Furies don't even know what gender Pegasus identifies with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:32:32-07:00","id":1408195,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth keeping in mind that while certain cultures have non-binary gender roles, it doesn't necessarily mean they're pro-trans (and that would work it's way into the views of different Tribes) in a broad sense. The Uktena most definitely have members that have lucked into the right mix of cultural heritage, beliefs, and being non-binary where they can be emotionally empowered by playing a gender role that's not man or woman. The Uktena are also going to be highly skeptical of allowing trans Garou that are simply looking for tolerance and lack any sort of legit connection to a given belief system that carved out a place for non-binary folks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T13:15:11-07:00","id":1408229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408164#post1408164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having NO modern, welcoming Black Furies would be as ridiculous as leaving the game's present-day date in 2003.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do think it'd be narratively appropriate for the Get of Fenrir or the Shadow Lords to be more welcoming of Trans people. Why don't you push for those tribes to accept trans people? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you want ALL werewolves and humans everywhere to keep the hate-filled bigotry of the 18th century, with no exceptions whatsoever, you should just play Werewolf: the Wild West. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Did I say that? No. Don't cloud facts with your feelings. </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's 2020. The setting will advance past 2003. There's no sense in pretending it won't or shouldn't... <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> If the modern world offends you so horribly, you don't have to play in it, or worry about a book set in the modern day.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>And in ten years it'll be 2030, and if there are any humans left after the apocalyptic war it'll be 2040 in 20 years. The only tribe that changes it's identity this fast is the glass walkers. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And what about this modern world? Do trans rights correlate to modernity? You seem to be under the mistaken impression that now is a good time. Relatively speaking, it might be. But it's not exactly good, is it? There are vocal advocates of trans rights, there are quite supporters of trans people, there are people who don't care about trans people, and there's a spectrum of disgust. Just because Trans people have more ground that they did does not mean they've claimed the field. For all you know in 10 years the radical push for a gender spectrum will be seen as a tragic fad (or heresy, looking at the current political trends) The point being: Should the Black Furies really put themselves into the here and now? Once they take the people in it's going to be an ordeal to get them out. Can the Black furies really do it with their totem spirit being who he is? Garou, except the glass walkers, are by their very nature conservative. No doubt there are many Black Furies who support trans people; They're mostly the young ones who have little say in how the tribe does things. It'd be intelectually dishonest to allow homid &quot;men&quot; in the tribe just because the trans movement has been in the spotlight of late: we're in the World of Darkness, not the World of Enlightenment. <br /> <br /> If you want to play a Male to female homid: Play a Silent Strider, play a Wendigo, an Uktena, a Silver Fang, A Child of Gaia, a Bone Gnawer, A Glass Walker, and If you're a trans lupus you can play a Red talon. The Black Furies; Bite the bullet and play a Metis, or have an easy time of it and play a Cis woman. WTA is not trans exclusive; Far from it. But that doesn't mean every organization should be inclusive, especially one who's whole gig originated as a TERF parody. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T13:28:50-07:00","id":1408231,"title":"","content":"The Silver Fangs don\u2019t seem like they would be trans friendly being a bunch of Aristocratitc douches with a obsession with Blood purity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:07:30-07:00","id":1408234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408229#post1408229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't you push for those tribes to accept trans people?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) This is push back against your focus on keeping the BFs TERF-y.<br /> <br /> 2) The BFs are the Tribe of gender politics, so they're the Tribe where this matters the most. All of the other Tribes have being trans as something that is incidental to your relationship with your Tribe.<br /> <br /> 3) As you seem to forget whenever it doesn't go in your favor, current feminism pushing back against the older feminism is punk/satire fuel that's strongest in the BFs compared to other parts of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that doesn't mean every organization should be inclusive, especially one who's whole gig originated as a TERF parody. </div> </div> </div>The BFs didn't originate as s TERF parody. They originated as a third wave feminist satirical critique of first and second wave feminism. The term TERF wasn't popularized until 2008. Obviously the sentiments behind it are far older, but TERF nonsense grew in response to the push to recognize trans identities... which wasn't really a big part of feminist debates in 1992.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:23:06-07:00","id":1408238,"title":"","content":"Okay, time to bring the Fury round-up I did; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980696#post980696\">Link.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Look into Fury views through books.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:33:07-07:00","id":1408241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408234#post1408234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) This is push back against your focus on keeping the BFs TERF-y.<br /> <br /> 2) The BFs are the Tribe of gender politics, so they're the Tribe where this matters the most. All of the other Tribes have being trans as something that is incidental to your relationship with your Tribe.<br /> <br /> 3) As you seem to forget whenever it doesn't go in your favor, current feminism pushing back against the older feminism is punk/satire fuel that's strongest in the BFs compared to other parts of the setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The BFs didn't originate as s TERF parody. They originated as a third wave feminist satirical critique of first and second wave feminism. The term TERF wasn't popularized until 2008. Obviously the sentiments behind it are far older, but TERF nonsense grew in response to the push to recognize trans identities... which wasn't really a big part of feminist debates in 1992.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the Black furies originated as a Satirical take on Second and third wave feminism?<br /> <br /> Where\u2019s that from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:49:01-07:00","id":1408268,"title":"","content":"The Black Furies originated as, mainly, a third wave feminist critique on second wave feminism. This seems.. painfully obvious if you understand the broad concepts of what each wave of feminism is about, and how historically they've related to each other. <br /> <br /> The leadership of the BFs was coded very strongly as reflecting the feminism of the &quot;60s.&quot; Women suffered a major setback in equality following WWII as they were expected to give up on careers that were more traditionally masculine that they made significant in-roads in due to the war, leading to reduced power in domestic relationship dynamics. The second wave feminist activism was heavily oriented around reclaiming &quot;motherhood&quot; as something women controlled and defined instead of something men defined for them (also leading to the origin of radical feminism as the desire for extreme societal reordering to dismantle the patriarchy). The rise of easy access to hormonal birth control, the free love movement, and the push for legalized abortions eventually coming to a head in Roe v. Wade, all focused the dominant feminism of the day on having a functional uterus.<br /> <br /> The young (aka PC) BFs were coded after the earlier third wave feminists largely before third wave was even a recognized thing (mostly the west cost feminist punks of the late 80s/early 90s). Third wave grew out of the discontent that during the late 70s/80s, the second wave feminist leaders basically acted like they'd won the moral argument and could focus on slow incrementalist change; while the anti-porn vs. sex-positive clashes left a whole generation of feminists without any clear movement to join that reflected current issues. Since third wave was so dominated by being highly critical of how second wave had been very successful for middle/upper class white cis-women, and did very little for all other women, it lacked significantly in cohesion (leading to fourth wave feminism's unification around intersectionality) as it was more opposition than movement with distinct goals.<br /> <br /> So, where's the claim from? It's from that being how the BFs were constructed as a Tribe (esp. their Camps) even if the books never calls any of this out by name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T16:30:11-07:00","id":1408276,"title":"","content":"Thankfully, unlike the CoG, their Revised Tribebook gave them an identity, purpose, and history that predated the 60s and made them feel actually ancient and mythological.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I think one way in which Furies would be centuries ahead of human 'feminism' is in their acceptance of Intersexed children as-is (at least, if they're born of two Garou). Pegasus would be <b>very</b> opposed to any surgery to castrate little children, and however strongly they supported the gender binary itself ancient Furies would look upon surgical alteration of children's genitals as the sort of atrocity they were created to avenge with bloody claws. I wouldn't be surprised if they thought circumcisn was a horrible thing, too. Well, especially after encountering the female genital mutilation.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean ancient Furies wouldn't assign a binary gender and then reject the homid and lupus cubs whom they decreed to be males (or in olden days... sacrifice them at birth). But I think the whole modern &quot;let's chop off the genitals of infants who can't possibly consent, in a futile attempt to force them to be heterosexual!&quot; movement would surprise and horrify Black Furies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-14-2020, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T03:01:58-07:00","id":1408325,"title":"","content":"That's the issue: the BF's are portrayed as ancient and magical: and yet a push to accept trans homids would date them so very modern. There might be good out of character reasons for a shift, but in-universe It's a terrible idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T04:44:12-07:00","id":1408334,"title":"","content":"Why?<br /> <br /> The idea that Garou &quot;can't&quot; keep up with human social trends isn't in the books (as opposed to don't want to), and Tribes like the BFs, GWs, and CoGs, are notable for their focus on keeping current as issues they care about change fairly rapidly.<br /> <br /> Garou aren't vampires where being born 75 years ago means you're still a baby in the eyes of most vampires. Anyone playing a starting level BF in a game that's set in 2020 is playing a character that grew up with third and fourth wave feminism (including third wave's increased advocacy for solidarity with the LGBTQ movement, and fourth wave's increased focus on intersectionality) being the normal of what feminism looks like &quot;on the ground&quot; even if their elders are more old school (just like feminists in the real world). Most of the Adren and Athros of the Tribe are also going to have grown up with third wave feminism either as it started or solidly part of their lives as second wave feminism would have been at least two generations back for them.<br /> <br /> It makes no in-universe sense that transwomen aren't part of the Tribe by 2020. We have the Millennial and Zoomer generations as the default PCs that have had enough time to get the Rank to try to initiate transwomen into the Tribe regardless of what their seniors think (keeping in mind that most second wave BFs are long dead now as old age isn't really a common thing for Garou and they're Boomers). Pegasus has no reason to completely reject transwomen (even if you want to say that Pegasus demands some level of transition or whatever rather than blanket acceptance).<br /> <br /> What makes sense, in-universe and out, is for the biggest philosophic struggle within the BFs to be about healing men instead of punishing them as the younger BFs are going to come in with attitudes more in-line with the CoGs regarding restorative justice and deprogramming toxic masculinity instead of treating men as bad simply because the patriarchy benefits them socioeconomically. That's where a lot of the struggle is, because that's where a lot of the lines between third and fourth wave get drawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T05:06:36-07:00","id":1408336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408325#post1408325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the issue: the BF's are portrayed as ancient and magical: and yet a push to accept trans homids would date them so very modern. There might be good out of character reasons for a shift, but in-universe It's a terrible idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually no, a lot of cultures had what we would call a Male to Female transsexuals<br /> <a href=\"http://bilerico.lgbtqnation.com/2008/02/transgender_history_trans_expression_in.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://bilerico.lgbtqnation.com/2008...ression_in.php</a><br /> <br /> It ain\u2019t a contemporary thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 08-15-2020, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T06:30:28-07:00","id":1408343,"title":"","content":"I can only say what Changing Ways says about this. Some Transwomen are already part of the tribe because the newest BF activly fought for them. The problem is not only about Feminism and Minority Fighting but the fact, that Garou are deep down Zealots for Gaia. If you would accept Transsexuality as part of a Garou, it means you accept that Gaia made a mistake which is what MWIS is saying if I understood him correct. Other tribes would accept Trans Garou too (I could there honestly imagine Get of Fenris because from my understanding the accept the strong are right) as on the same status as a Metis. On other Tribes those Garou are immedeataly slayn for their sacrileg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T14:41:39-07:00","id":1408410,"title":"","content":"The Garou are religious zealots as a culture, but their belief system does not hinge on Gaia being infallible like the Abrahamic creator.<br /> <br /> The idea that transness only happens because of a &quot;mistake&quot; or a &quot;failing&quot; is a conceit of human cultural bias; and is also fairly modern. Nature does not give a single shit about humans that think that the &quot;natural&quot; order is that you have some creatures born male, and others born female. Some things in nature follow that, and most do something different on a vast spectrum of variations (and that's just looking at sexual reproductive life!). All evidence points to humans as having an inherent minority of non-conformists (not just regarding gender), and that for most of the time humanity has existed, humanity chose to create cultural norms that elevated socially productive non-conformity; not denounce it as a flaw. It's easy to make the case that this acceptable non-conformity is one of humanity's greatest strengths as it gives space in human cultures for radical thinking and thus greater social adaptability.<br /> <br /> Gaia (and whoever else) created the Fera out of mixing the spiritual natures of humanity and animals. The human mind is always a keep thing that's considered a positive that the human side brings to the table: complex cultural thinking beyond what other animals do without the rigidity of eusocial behaviors. Gaia wanted the Garou to have humanity's ability to transmit complex cultural behaviors, and the ability to reconcile non-conformity.<br /> <br /> Or there's a simple answer: If trans Garou are a mistake, so are the Ragabash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T15:42:49-07:00","id":1408415,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> It seems you did not understood me or I failed an english skill test. In Changeing Ways it is said not from a narrative but a fact point, that Garou will slay other Garou because they say they are born in the wrong body and because of this made a sacrileg on Gaia because Gaia thought something about that you are now in this body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T15:52:01-07:00","id":1408416,"title":"","content":"Some other points for your consideration:<br /> <br /> There's an absolutely huge amount of trans players playing tabletop. I've seldom seen a game without one at the table. But how many Trans people are there in the wider world, of which the World of Darkness is based on? Trans people are a very small minority; Gaia's chosen are a very small minority. Gaia's chosen trans people are going to be extremely few realistically. This leads on to the next point:<br /> <br /> While A Black Fury might fight for trans rights, does that mean she wants trans people on her team? This is the World of Darkness after all; Does she care enough to go against her elders? (and yes, while elders might be a minority in Garou society, Garou society is hierarchical and they have a lot of sway) Perhaps she views trans people as soft things to be protected and coddled? I mean, the trans people I know well (by no means a huge sample size) are... On the inside, really nice. On the surface, they push a lot of people away, and they seem to have a lot of comorbidity issues.They also tend to be the most moral players at the table. Now yeah this is just my personal experience and I'm aware I've probably got some confirmation bias with trans people I know less well, but they're the last people I'd imagine as rage-fueled murder machines, Isn't it likely that the Black Furies have the same perception? I mean, looking at trans people in the military (A messy topic and a lot of it goes against my argument, but I try to be objective) it seems to be fine (most people who join the military want to be there) but there's still some heavy biases both for and against that (I'll note that one group have suggested a high estimate that USA about 21% of trans people have served in the military: That's 1 in 5. I don't know if I should trust this study, but I imagine when people are talking about trans people in the military in a negative sense they're talking about the other 4 trans people*.<br /> (*Yeah, 4/5 is not reasonable; If 21% joined the military I'd imagine there'd be at least an equal amount who gravitated towards other macho jobs instead... The trans people I've played with were decisively not these people... but also, are such people likely to seek out the Black Furies for membership rather than another tribe? it seems the Get of Fenrir would hold more appeal now that I think about it)<br /> <br /> And yeah, the Comorbidity. Gender disphoria comes with a lot of problems, most notably a high suicide rate. Gender disphoria is fucking horrible. The misery it causes likely feeds banes and fuels harrano. This fuels this idea that trans people should be protected and makes them not the most desirable tribe initiates.<br /> <br /> Then there's the last issue: You, the reader, might see the Black Furies as the Champions of Gender, but your character probably isn't. It's difficult to change your reputation so quickly, and when it comes to pups, a lot of Garou aren't going to want to point a good prospective initiate in the other direction. The Black Furies aren't an easy-going tribe: I'd rank them as No.4 in the 'Which tribe has the most enemies' ranking, and that's impressive because they're one of the smaller tribes. If you live off the reservation, When you go through the first change, and you are found, you aren't given an unbiased list, If you don't have the kind of pure breed that'd attract the demand of a tribe, the first thing your finders will do is try recruit you and sell you on their tribe alone, and failing that the other locals will try to recruit you, and failing that they'll point you to people they like. The tribes that like the Black furies tend to be the ones that'd accept trans members.<br /> <br /> So, you have the Black furies. There's plenty of reasons for them to fight on behalf of the Trans community, but for them allowing trans homids is only a moral victory, it isn't a practical victory. The practical logistics and value of the move would be... debatable; You aren't getting many more members and the ones who do seek you out amongst all the tribes tend not to be the macho-murder-machine women you're looking for. You encourage in-fighting in the tribe, you have to go through a whole load of bullshit sorting through spiritual contracts, The male-sex characters who join up will likely be confused with the metis who have long been associated as the only male members of the tribe.<br /> <br /> In universe, it's a terrible, terrible idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-15-2021, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T16:57:19-07:00","id":1408418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408415#post1408415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> It seems you did not understood me or I failed an english skill test. In Changeing Ways it is said not from a narrative but a fact point, that Garou will slay other Garou because they say they are born in the wrong body and because of this made a sacrileg on Gaia because Gaia thought something about that you are now in this body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that statement was literally inserted into the book by some edgelord muppet at Paradox White Wolf after the book was written and submitted by the Developer and Writing Team.<br /> <br /> Which is a terrible shame because the one book in recent years that even mentions Trans individuals is an untrustworthy source that contradicts itself every few pages because its not the book that was originally written.<br /> <br /> Now I know what I've been using the last 20 odd years, is that Trans, intersex etc. folks are accepted by Pegasus but that was simply because I asked Ethan about it when he was Developer and he stated that of course they were accepted. But finding book references either way is damn difficult.....I've spent the last few days reading through my entire WtA collection to find a Trans reference that intersected with the BFs and there simply isn't one ( quite possible I missed one I was getting pretty tired and sore eyes towards the end). Theres a couple of throw away references to Trans individuals in the CoGs, but nothing either way in regard to Furies. <br /> <br /> The IC nature of books doesn't really help either, theres an OOC side column in the BF Revised Tribebook stating that Pegasus is of indeterminate gender, neither male, female or neuter. And then every IC character reference is to her as She which continues on through the *20 books.<br /> <br /> For myself, I'm going with what Ethan said and what I've been using in my games as none of it is contradicted by anything in the books except Changing Ways which is an untrustworthy source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T16:58:39-07:00","id":1408419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408415#post1408415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> It seems you did not understood me or I failed an english skill test. In Changeing Ways it is said not from a narrative but a fact point, that Garou will slay other Garou because they say they are born in the wrong body and because of this made a sacrileg on Gaia because Gaia thought something about that you are now in this body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was added to the book over the author and developer's objections. <br /> <br /> Changing Ways 20th might be an official book, but a lot of us ignore it because it's full of a lot of garbage. If W5 was in the hands of the same people that added a these sorts of stupid ideas to that book, I would have zero hope it could turn out well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408416#post1408416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But how many Trans people are there in the wider world, of which the World of Darkness is based on?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter. Some of them are going to be Garou, and some of them are going to want to be Black Furies. Barring the PCs from playing it because it's rare would mean baring playing any supernaturals because those are all rare in the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While A Black Fury might fight for trans rights, does that mean she wants trans people on her team? </div> </div> </div>The majority of them by 2020 would answer with a very strong yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does she care enough to go against her elders? </div> </div> </div>Yes, if the Garou didn't care enough to push against their elders, the game would be boring as fuck. All the punk and satire would be dead and it would boil down to playing soldiers &quot;just following orders,&quot; as they enact violence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps she views trans people as soft things to be protected and coddled? </div> </div> </div>No, because she's been hearing that about herself her whole life and wouldn't want to inflict that sort of patronizing bullshit on others. The Black Furies have been fighting this attitude about women for thousands of years, they're not going to perpetuate it on others as a generality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ... but also, are such people likely to seek out the Black Furies for membership rather than another tribe? </div> </div> </div>A Tribe focused on fighting for equality and diversity in the face of the very patriarchal Garou Nation? Yeah, that's something a lot of trans people would be down for if they found out the were also Garou. It's not like joining that Black Furies means abandoning being a fighter and only the Fenrir have claim over that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The misery it causes likely feeds banes and fuels harrano. This fuels this idea that trans people should be protected and makes them not the most desirable tribe initiates. </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, the BF use their rites specifically designed to help people with mental trauma to help their trans sisters through such matters so they can be their full powerful selves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You, the reader, might see the Black Furies as the Champions of Gender, but your character probably isn't. </div> </div> </div>Me, the reader, sees the Black Furies as philosophically having the ideals of feminism even if they're made up of flawed individuals that vary in how well they live up to such ideals; just like any other group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, you have the Black furies. There's plenty of reasons for them to fight on behalf of the Trans community, but for them allowing trans homids is only a moral victory, it isn't a practical victory. </div> </div> </div>Because the Garou are so focused on purely practical rationales for what they do?<br /> <br /> And it's a practical victory even if a small one, that literally has no actual practical cost to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...macho-murder-machine women you're looking for. </div> </div> </div>The fact that you typed this phrase very much calls into question your understanding of the Black Furies and feminism as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You encourage in-fighting in the tribe, you have to go through a whole load of bullshit sorting through spiritual contracts, The male-sex characters who join up will likely be confused with the metis who have long been associated as the only male members of the tribe. </div> </div> </div>The increased in-fighting is effectively over the second Pegasus empowers an initiation of a trans woman Garou into the Tribe because the Elders might not like it, but Pegasus outranks them. Then it's back to the normal levels of in-fighting already present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In universe, it's a terrible, terrible idea. </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. You have yet to present any case that actually supports this position, or even refute all the reasons it's a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T17:09:45-07:00","id":1408422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_conta