ey found out the were also Garou. It's not like joining that Black Furies means abandoning being a fighter and only the Fenrir have claim over that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or, you know, the BF use their rites specifically designed to help people with mental trauma to help their trans sisters through such matters so they can be their full powerful selves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Me, the reader, sees the Black Furies as philosophically having the ideals of feminism even if they're made up of flawed individuals that vary in how well they live up to such ideals; just like any other group.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because the Garou are so focused on purely practical rationales for what they do?<br /> <br /> And it's a practical victory even if a small one, that literally has no actual practical cost to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The fact that you typed this phrase very much calls into question your understanding of the Black Furies and feminism as a whole.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The increased in-fighting is effectively over the second Pegasus empowers an initiation of a trans woman Garou into the Tribe because the Elders might not like it, but Pegasus outranks them. Then it's back to the normal levels of in-fighting already present.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, it isn't. You have yet to present any case that actually supports this position, or even refute all the reasons it's a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know we've butted heads occasionally over the years, but thankyou for this post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":