from playing it because it's rare would mean baring playing any supernaturals because those are all rare in the WoD.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The majority of them by 2020 would answer with a very strong yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, if the Garou didn't care enough to push against their elders, the game would be boring as fuck. All the punk and satire would be dead and it would boil down to playing soldiers &amp;quot;just following orders,&amp;quot; as they enact violence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, because she's been hearing that about herself her whole life and wouldn't want to inflict that sort of patronizing bullshit on others. The Black Furies have been fighting this attitude about women for thousands of years, they're not going to perpetuate it on others as a generality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A Tribe focused on fighting for equality and diversity in the face of the very patriarchal Garou Nation? Yeah, that's something a lot of trans people would be down for if they found out the were also Garou. It's not like joining that Black Furies means abandoning being a fighter and only the Fenrir have claim over that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or, you know, the BF use their rites specifically designed to help people with mental trauma to help their trans sisters through such matters so they can be their full powerful selves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Me, the reader, sees the Black Furies as philosophically having the ideals of feminism even if they're made up of flawed individuals that vary in how well they live up to such ideals; just like any other group.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because the Garou are so focused on purely practical rationales for what they do?<br /> <br /> And it's a practical victory even if a small one, that literally has no actual practical cost to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The fact that you typed this phrase very much calls into question your understanding of the Black Furies and feminism as a whole.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The increased in-fighting is effectively over the second Pegasus empowers an initiation of a trans woman Garou into the Tribe because the Elders might not like it, but Pegasus outranks them. Then it's back to the normal levels of in-fighting already present.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, it isn't. You have yet to present any case that actually supports this position, or even refute all the reasons it's a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with everything you said here, except I never read Changing Ways so idk firsthand what it says and why certain parts were added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T18:07:03-07:00","id":1408433,"title":"","content":"I'm very sad to see the direction this thread has gone for the last few pages, forsaken is a cool game with a lot of cool ideas for getting into the headspace of primal spirit hunters and apex predators that need to balance their human lives that I think would make for a great addition to WtA, at the very least for helping get into the ground-level headspace of the player characters.<br /> <br /> I am going to say that as a transwoman who plays with a number of people, both queer and not, in gaming spaces, and who has played werewolf with other queer people that making the Black furies behave as transphobic is terrible game design. Period. Separate and apart from any in-setting justifications or lack thereof, it is terrible game design.<br /> The players at the table and the game designers are real people, who are genuinely affected by these issues and will look at the game as an expression of that. And writing a game where your punk-feminist werewolves fighting against capitalist exploitation and demons are universally terfs by divine decree is wildly out of touch with their market audience and the WoD playerbase, particularly right now when major governments and notable celebrity figures are making rounds trying to hurt transfolks.<br /> It's also a bad idea where actual gameplay experience is concerned, if I am walking into every werewolf game with an X-card handy for the fact that a Black-Fury <i>might appear at all in any capacity </i>because I'd be afraid of being the target of a simulated hate crime, that is bad game design, for much the same reason that making Silver-Fangs Alt-righters would be bad game design, it's offputting to the playerbase, undermines the core premise the game is about and makes it hard to develop a narrative or build characters. As a storyteller, one should not need to preemptively ban players from using the core character options for fear of genuinely hurting the players at their table, that should be an isolated and highly situational occurrence (No werespiders around serious arachnaphobes) rather than a general requirement for the game to be used at a public space (no bigotry). Most players (especially queer gamers) will be drawn to the game to rage <i>against </i>hatred, stupidity, and bigotry in the real world, not to embody it. That's a fine line WtA has always walked and the line has only grown finer in recent years.<br /> <br /> Regardless of any history the <i>game</i> might have, the <i>game</i> is coming out now, when this is a hot issue and queer folks make up a larger than ever demographic in tabletop gaming. Making any group in this actively undermine the <i>game</i>'s core premise isn't just wildly out of touch with your target audience, it's also stupid from a marketing standpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 08-15-2020, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T18:50:36-07:00","id":1408438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408416#post1408416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some other points for your consideration:<br /> <br /> There's an absolutely amount of trans players playing tabletop. I've seldom seen a game without one at the table. But how many Trans people are there in the wider world, of which the World of Darkness is based on? Trans people are a very small minority; Gaia's chosen are a very small minority. Gaia's chosen trans people are going to be extremely few realistically. This leads on to the next point:</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">*snip*</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This entire post was just a terrible examination of the subject from top to bottom. I understand the argument that Garou may be a bunch of horrible transphobes and reactionaries but this plays into a lot of things that need to be handled with great care.<br /> <br /> Also, the matter should be handled by whatever makes the players (trans and otherwise) feel comfortable and enjoy themselves at the game.<br /> <br /> It's also wildly off topic.<br /> <br /> Please everyone drop it now. The subject is worth a thread but only in the context of what would best be handling the subject in a way that is enjoyable to players and gaming.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-16-2020, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T19:46:25-07:00","id":1408442,"title":"","content":"Okay, I would like some Lore changes, and having more diverse writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T20:17:28-07:00","id":1408446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408442#post1408442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I would like some Lore changes, and having more diverse writers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Second is already taken care of if you check out the writers list from Hunters Entertainment.<br /> <br /> I'd like sensible progressions of the Lore changes already enacted in WtA Rev. and W20 ( Except CW).<br /> <br /> WtF is a good game but both groups of fans lose out if the two games are brought too close together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T01:02:06-07:00","id":1408463,"title":"","content":"So like... <br /> WoD combat was pretty simulationist till V5. If you had the right storyteller, you could make the game into an MMA simulator. , If you had your average -knows-nothing-bout-fighting storyteller, you still had a lot more to work with than, say, the more complicated versions of DnD. It's such a detailed system that I die a little inside every time the player just says &quot;I hit him&quot; for their actions each turn (though that is a perfectly viable strategy). Werewolf went further than vampire in that you had multiple forms and pack tactics (also all the weapons had different difficulties which is kinda stupid) and a good chance that whatever you're fighting will have tentacles or extra limbs or something special. <br /> <br /> V5, the combat system is geared towards getting combat out of the way. It's very simplistic, all the reasons I liked WoD combat are gone (Yeah, the new system is a lot faster, but so were my houserules, and I didn't sacrifice anything with those) All the combat looks like mook combat. <br /> But W:tF is, to my knowledge, a lot less combat heavy than W:tA. Now the idea of looking for a spirit's banes isn't bad but Garou are meant to be musclebound meatheads that only need to do that for really strong spirits they can't gangbang to death in the first place without taking loses. You aren't all theurges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T01:46:58-07:00","id":1408467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408463#post1408463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But W:tF is, to my knowledge, a lot less combat heavy than W:tA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the differences in their systems, Forsaken is still a pretty violence heavy game. The Uratha generally hunt down dangerous things that can fight back. The Uratha have to hunt regularly too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but Garou are meant to be musclebound meatheads.... </div> </div> </div>Citation needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You aren't all theurges. </div> </div> </div>No, but, they're not all Ahrouns either. And Ahrouns are expected to learn how to be effective combat leaders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T06:21:55-07:00","id":1408482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408446#post1408446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Second is already taken care of if you check out the writers list from Hunters Entertainment.<br /> <br /> I'd like sensible progressions of the Lore changes already enacted in WtA Rev. and W20 ( Except CW).<br /> <br /> WtF is a good game but both groups of fans lose out if the two games are brought too close together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes more diverse writers the Pure tribes won\u2019t be cringe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T06:34:50-07:00","id":1408484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408482#post1408482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes more diverse writers the Pure tribes won\u2019t be cringe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny story. The first time I bought a Forsaken product was by accident. I was pretty new to gaming and was just getting into W:tA. So my boyfriend at the time took me to the local gaming store in his town and sitting on the shelf was a copy of the Pure sourcebook. I looked at it really fast (he was in a hurry), saw the title and saw it had werewolves on the cover, and I thought it was a book about the Pure Ones for Apocalypse! It wasn\u2019t till I got in the car and started flipping thru it that I realized it was for a totally different game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T06:36:51-07:00","id":1408485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408484#post1408484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny story. The first time I bought a Forsaken product was by accident. I was pretty new to gaming and was just getting into W:tA. So my boyfriend at the time took me to the local gaming store in his town and sitting on the shelf was a copy of the Pure sourcebook. I looked at it really fast (he was in a hurry), saw the title and saw it had werewolves on the cover, and I thought it was a book about the Pure Ones for Apocalypse! It wasn\u2019t till I got in the car and started flipping thru it that I realized it was for a totally different game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, that most have soured your experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T06:40:32-07:00","id":1408487,"title":"","content":"It was defo not what I expected lol. But it got me curious about Forsaken and I checked out some of the lore and even though I never actually played it I still think it\u2019s a pretty cool game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T11:42:54-07:00","id":1408524,"title":"","content":"One of my biggest fears with W5, is that they will just out and out drop lupus and metis. I know it seems like a weird fear, but given the more ground-level focus of later WoD things, I feel they might be dropped as 'too hard to play' or like in Chronicles of Darkness, just impossible to use in the system. Especially for lupus, they might be seen as 'too goofy' or 'furry bait.'<br /> <br /> Or, just the writers being uncomfortable with the idea.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the reason I don't want them to be dropped, is that they bring a sense of completeness to the setting and the animal to the garou. A Hunter in the Darkness will always have grown a human and chosen to be atavistic. A lupus just -is- of the nature.<br /> <br /> Metis, on the other hand, serve as a way to look into the garou culture through a deeper lens.<br /> <br /> Plus, in utterly personal reason, I like playing non-human character trying to understand humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 08-16-2020, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T12:14:02-07:00","id":1408526,"title":"","content":"Yeah V5 seemed to want to get rid of all the silly stuff, in Vampire and make it a serious horror game, by taking out all the fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T13:42:56-07:00","id":1408569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408526#post1408526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah V5 seemed to want to get rid of all the silly stuff, in Vampire and make it a serious horror game, by taking out all the fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's uh... a lot to unpack in terms of irony. <br /> V5 is plenty silly. on a content to silly ratio, it's easily the silliest vampire game so far, perhaps edging out the rest of the WoD: Changeling doesn't even have that kind of sillyness. <br /> <br /> Brujah were at one point 'triggered'. The hunger system all too often devolves games into a comedy of errors, the writing and the art...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T16:10:00-07:00","id":1408607,"title":"","content":"Okay i guess it\u2019s because I don\u2019t like he Humor. It\u2019s a bunch of trying to act like a internet conversation like tumblr or the least bad parts of 4chan, amd it just doesn\u2019t work, It is a attempt to sound personable. And I am sick of that type of meme, relatable humor.<br /> <br /> Requiem second edition did it and I do not like those sections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T16:59:02-07:00","id":1408614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408463#post1408463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now the idea of looking for a spirit's banes isn't bad but Garou are meant to be musclebound meatheads that only need to do that for really strong spirits they can't gangbang to death in the first place without taking loses. You aren't all theurges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny that you left out the Ragabash as clever. Or the Philodox as cerebral. Or the Galliard as being a bit of both, capable of messing with minds as a matter of course. Even the Ahrouns, too, have to change functions into leaders as they advance in society. Meatheads don't last long unless someone good at politics is propping them up and dripping policy decisions toward them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T18:55:29-07:00","id":1408624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408524#post1408524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my biggest fears with W5, is that they will just out and out drop lupus and metis. I know it seems like a weird fear, but given the more ground-level focus of later WoD things, I feel they might be dropped as 'too hard to play' or like in Chronicles of Darkness, just impossible to use in the system. Especially for lupus, they might be seen as 'too goofy' or 'furry bait.'<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, the whole game kinda is 'furry bait'. I'd wager most players are fine with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T19:04:24-07:00","id":1408627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408624#post1408624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, the whole game kinda is 'furry bait'. I'd wager most players are fine with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd think so, but I have seen people freak out about lupus (and one time metis.) Some people truly seemed to want a gory werewolf RP and so the -concept- of a lupus is shock jockeying for them. I don't bring this up because I enjoy talking about it, but its something I've seen is an issue.<br /> <br /> The other, though not from the writers, is the 'lupus should be EXTREMELY hard to play because they have 5 gnosis' mentality. Instead of simply house-ruling the gnosis amount to sensible numbers, people are expected to have a biologist level understanding of wolves when playing a lupus. And the character cannot grow from that, ever.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T19:22:20-07:00","id":1408628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408627#post1408627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd think so, but I have seen people freak out about lupus (and one time metis.) Some people truly seemed to want a gory werewolf RP and so the -concept- of a lupus is shock jockeying for them. I don't bring this up because I enjoy talking about it, but its something I've seen is an issue.<br /> <br /> The other, though not from the writers, is the 'lupus should be EXTREMELY hard to play because they have 5 gnosis' mentality. Instead of simply house-ruling the gnosis amount to sensible numbers, people are expected to have a biologist level understanding of wolves when playing a lupus. And the character cannot grow from that, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... different strokes, I guess? It's not that I don't understand why people could be squicked out by the concept, but losing the wolfwere one would cut off some rather interesting angles. V5 is most fun when it's inclusive. Or so it seems to me.<br /> <br /> Regarding the second point, is that a ST thing? I remember several lupus template characters who were barely wolves at all. And one that was outright called a dog through his entire entry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26275,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","user":"Konigheim Horror","date":". 08-17-2020, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T20:19:45-07:00","id":1408642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408526#post1408526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah V5 seemed to want to get rid of all the silly stuff, in Vampire and make it a serious horror game, by taking out all the fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No edition warring. The edition wars ended with the destruction of Praxis and the Khitomer Accords.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T20:22:10-07:00","id":1408643,"title":"","content":"Also, I point out;<br /> <br /> * Lupus or &quot;Wolfweres&quot; are a thing D&amp;D games did just fine. Harkon Lukas, Galliard Lupus in Ravenloft. They're wolves that become humans with human intelligence and huge past lives of knowledge.<br /> <br /> * Metis are created by two Homids having sex in human form as much as anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-16-2020, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T23:31:58-07:00","id":1408656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408614#post1408614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny that you left out the Ragabash as clever. Or the Philodox as cerebral. Or the Galliard as being a bit of both, capable of messing with minds as a matter of course. Even the Ahrouns, too, have to change functions into leaders as they advance in society. Meatheads don't last long unless someone good at politics is propping them up and dripping policy decisions toward them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're taking me far to literally. <br /> I just meant that the best option for garou is usually overwhelming force, and it'd be strange if they lost their advantage so that they were pushed towards 'cerebral' dealings with wyrm spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T02:35:22-07:00","id":1408680,"title":"","content":"&quot;Overwhelming force,&quot; doesn't mean, &quot;fight stupid.&quot; Assuming all sides in a fight are going to be coming to blows, overwhelming force is always the best option, but who has the overwhelming force isn't just who has the most numbers, or the biggest bruisers, or whatever. &quot;Cerebral&quot; approaches mean using force multipliers to increase how much stronger your force is compared to your opponents. Studying your enemy, finding out their weaknesses, picking the best battlegrounds... these are all &quot;cerebral&quot; parts of obtaining overwhelming force. And they're all plenty part of WtA already.<br /> <br /> The Garou as supposed to be so dangerous not just because of their raw physical power, but because of their instinctive skill at operating as a group in combat; aka fighting smarter.<br /> <br /> The game is also very clear that trying to beat the Wyrm by hitting it as hard as possible as often as possible hasn't actually been a winning move for the Garou. The most successful moments for them are when they use all the tools at their disposal - including those brains of theirs - to defeat the Wyrm on a more holistic level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T02:54:59-07:00","id":1408682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408643#post1408643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I point out;<br /> <br /> * Lupus or &quot;Wolfweres&quot; are a thing D&amp;D games did just fine. Harkon Lukas, Galliard Lupus in Ravenloft. They're wolves that become humans with human intelligence and huge past lives of knowledge.<br /> <br /> * Metis are created by two Homids having sex in human form as much as anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, it should not be an issue at all. But either its due to people freaking out about furries (in a werewolf game...yeah) or trying to put their brains too deep into the concept, I have witnessed a few strong reactions towards the existence of lupus.<br /> <br /> Related to this thread, even the Forsaken&lt;---&gt;Apocalypse conversion guide was uncomfortable with the idea and pretty much went &quot;uhh, they are rare because they die from exposure as hishu after changing.&quot; Not knocking down the author, but it was clear the other breeds were not a big focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T05:07:13-07:00","id":1408691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408680#post1408680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Overwhelming force,&quot; doesn't mean, &quot;fight stupid.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>We've moved on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The game is also very clear that trying to beat the Wyrm by hitting it as hard as possible as often as possible hasn't actually been a winning move for the Garou. The most successful moments for them are when they use all the tools at their disposal - including those brains of theirs - to defeat the Wyrm on a more holistic level. </div> </div> </div>But if you imply the Garou have been fighting so cleverly all this time then one has to wonder why they're losing so hard.<br /> <br /> A big part of Garou being so dangerous is that they are innately terrifying on a physical level. They're average is neither worse nor better than your average soldier or vampire neonate. Perhaps the less cunning die off a little quicker due to the constant war, so they might be a little above average, or luna's blessings make them a little above average, their ability to change form gives them more oppertunities to leverage cunning, but it doesn't make them more cunning. A First Team or Sabbat pack can be equally cunning. But In scenarios where both sides have excellent plans or both sides have dropped the ball, the Lupines are feared because they're usually the ones winning through sheer physicality. They are give or take four hundred kilo masses of muscle and fur and claw that moves real fast.<br /> And in the umbra, they're often fighting titanic creatures.<br /> <br /> So, just saying 'Huh, werewolves are great because they're strategists&quot; is terribly reductionist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T05:29:16-07:00","id":1408692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408682#post1408682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely, it should not be an issue at all. But either its due to people freaking out about furries (in a werewolf game...yeah) or trying to put their brains too deep into the concept, I have witnessed a few strong reactions towards the existence of lupus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think it would be more the... well, the having sex with an animal thing that freaks people out. Homid Garou + Lupus kinfolk = Lupus Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T05:35:08-07:00","id":1408696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408642#post1408642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No edition warring. The edition wars ended with the destruction of Praxis and the Khitomer Accords.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Why does this sound like some propaganda a NWO MiB or Elder Tradition Mage would say?<br /> But in all seriousness I have never heard about it before.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408692#post1408692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd think it would be more the... well, the having sex with an animal thing that freaks people out. Homid Garou + Lupus kinfolk = Lupus Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which whas even described in CW as something that freaks modern Garou out despite it should actually be totally natural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 08-17-2020, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:06:34-07:00","id":1408706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408692#post1408692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd think it would be more the... well, the having sex with an animal thing that freaks people out. Homid Garou + Lupus kinfolk = Lupus Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's it, but it isn't just with homid+wolf kin, it is sometimes werewolf+wolf kin that makes people react to it.<br /> <br /> I mainly pointed this out, because as above post noted even Changing Ways already was treating the situation as 'gross' and uncomfortable. Hopefully in W5, the writers will not follow that route and address lupus like most books have done in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 08-17-2020, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:27:04-07:00","id":1408708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408680#post1408680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Overwhelming force,&amp;quot; doesn't mean, &amp;quot;fight stupid.&amp;quot; Assuming all sides in a fight are going to be coming to blows, overwhelming force is always the best option, but who has the overwhelming force isn't just who has the most numbers, or the biggest bruisers, or whatever. &amp;quot;Cerebral&amp;quot; approaches mean using force multipliers to increase how much stronger your force is compared to your opponents. Studying your enemy, finding out their weaknesses, picking the best battlegrounds... these are all &amp;quot;cerebral&amp;quot; parts of obtaining overwhelming force. And they're all plenty part of WtA already.<br /> <br /> The Garou as supposed to be so dangerous not just because of their raw physical power, but because of their instinctive skill at operating as a group in combat; aka fighting smarter.<br /> <br /> The game is also very clear that trying to beat the Wyrm by hitting it as hard as possible as often as possible hasn't actually been a winning move for the Garou. The most successful moments for them are when they use all the tools at their disposal - including those brains of theirs - to defeat the Wyrm on a more holistic level.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can\u2019t Defeat the Wyrm unless you deal with things that feed the Wyrm. Pollution,Homelessness,domestic abuse,<br /> <br /> The Wyrm feeds those things and in turn it feeds them, amd you can\u2019t just claw your way out of the force of destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:37:54-07:00","id":1408711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408708#post1408708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can\u2019t Defeat the Wyrm unless you deal with things that feed the Wyrm. Pollution,Homelessness,domestic abuse,<br /> <br /> The Wyrm feeds those things and in turn it feeds them, amd you can\u2019t just claw your way out of the force of destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the point of the setting, the ancestors were busy fighting their own wars and now the world is doomed. Especially in w20 and revised, there is a VERY strong &quot;we cannot beat this up to defeat this&quot; mentality. Which puts some of the more direct tribes in a bad place, especially Red Talons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:42:07-07:00","id":1408712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408706#post1408706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's it, but it isn't just with homid+wolf kin, it is sometimes werewolf+wolf kin that makes people react to it.<br /> <br /> I mainly pointed this out, because as above post noted even Changing Ways already was treating the situation as 'gross' and uncomfortable. Hopefully in W5, the writers will not follow that route and address lupus like most books have done in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games breeding goes as thus: The homid shall cleave to the human, and the lupus shall cleave to the wolf. Those that go against this will be shunned. End of Story...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:57:16-07:00","id":1408720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408712#post1408712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my games breeding goes as thus: The homid shall cleave to the human, and the lupus shall cleave to the wolf. Those that go against this will be shunned. End of Story...</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you need to either adjust the number of Lupi or have way more wolves in your setting. Because there are just so many lupus kinfolk and from normal canon you are desparate enough breed with every wolf you can so the number of wolves and better the number of lupus kinfolk and Garou will increase. Because if the animal of the shapeshifters die out, it is done for the Fera race because the Fera are not just humans that turn into animals.<br /> <br /> Something like this is even exlained in setting guide for ascension where first half is even giving advice how to define a world of darkness. Such &quot;small&quot; shifts can do a great of difference in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T08:23:11-07:00","id":1408721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408720#post1408720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then you need to either adjust the number of Lupi or have way more wolves in your setting. Because there are just so many lupus kinfolk and from normal canon you are desparate enough breed with every wolf you can so the number of wolves and better the number of lupus kinfolk and Garou will increase. Because if the animal of the shapeshifters die out, it is done for the Fera race because the Fera are not just humans that turn into animals.<br /> <br /> Something like this is even exlained in setting guide for ascension where first half is even giving advice how to define a world of darkness. Such &quot;small&quot; shifts can do a great of difference in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with you, it should be noted that if people are uncomfortable with the idea of homid+wolf kin, it is best not to push it.<br /> <br /> In the end, we are playing a fantasy game, and thus it is easier to just handwave stuff for those players who actually do feel uncomfortable with the topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T08:25:12-07:00","id":1408723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408696#post1408696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why does this sound like some propaganda a NWO MiB or Elder Tradition Mage would say?<br /> But in all seriousness I have never heard about it before.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Happiness is Mandatory.<br /> <br /> The Beatings will Continue until Morale Improves<br /> <br /> But in more seriousness, Onyx Path Publishing does Classic WoD, Chronicles of Darkness, and V5 so it welcomes fans of all. We're trying to make a good place for all of them to gather.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T12:11:57-07:00","id":1408759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408691#post1408691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've moved on.</div> </div> </div> </div>You want to move on ran than own up to a bad point. &quot;We&quot; doesn't apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if you imply the Garou have been fighting so cleverly all this time then one has to wonder why they're losing so hard. </div> </div> </div>Not really? The books are plenty clear on this. The Garou are really good at winning battles, are really bad at winning wars (mostly because they're bad at setting goals for wars besides winning battles, and have a bad history of picking the wrong people to go to war with).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A big part of Garou being so dangerous is that they are innately terrifying on a physical level. </div> </div> </div>That's generally more the perception of them from other gamelines that don't have as potent innate physical powers and have to rely more on bought powers for in-person conflict.<br /> <br /> The Garou's primary antagonists are very much designed so that there are plenty of equally dangerous physical threats as them out there.<br /> <br /> Of course, in regards to the topic of seeing more Forsaken stuff in Apocalypse, this isn't really any different between the two games (obviously some mechanical sticking points). The Uratha can all shift into extremely potent physical forms that make them easily more dangerous than most things in a fight that aren't built specifically for combat, and get even scarier if they buy combat boosting stuff, but there's plenty out there that can match them if built for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're average is neither worse nor better than your average soldier or vampire neonate. Perhaps the less cunning die off a little quicker due to the constant war, so they might be a little above average, or luna's blessings make them a little above average, their ability to change form gives them more oppertunities to leverage cunning, but it doesn't make them more cunning. </div> </div> </div>You're skipping a lot of things it seems because you're focused on individual powers. As an example, every Garou pack gain at least one (if not multiple) Pack Tactics as part of the package of forming a pack. Nobody else (not even Sabbat) get free special combat maneuvers for using group tactics.<br /> <br /> And, of course, the broader point on how cunning the Garou can be, is that they've got the Auspices, most of which are more &quot;cerebral&quot; in their approach to things; esp. when Tribes get factored in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, just saying 'Huh, werewolves are great because they're strategists&quot; is terribly reductionist. </div> </div> </div>Good thing nobody said that. What you're being pushed back on is your assumption that a more Forsaken-like W5 is going to mean that the Garou aren't going to be physical powerhouses (which doesn't check out because the Uratha are such as well), and that somehow it's going to force the Garou to be more &quot;cerebral&quot; in their approach (something the Garou are already more so than you seem to acknowledge, and something the books repeatedly point out they need to be more so if they want to actually win).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408708#post1408708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can\u2019t Defeat the Wyrm unless you deal with things that feed the Wyrm. Pollution,Homelessness,domestic abuse,<br /> <br /> The Wyrm feeds those things and in turn it feeds them, amd you can\u2019t just claw your way out of the force of destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>As illustrated well right here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T12:20:05-07:00","id":1408761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408706#post1408706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's it, but it isn't just with homid+wolf kin, it is sometimes werewolf+wolf kin that makes people react to it.<br /> <br /> I mainly pointed this out, because as above post noted even Changing Ways already was treating the situation as 'gross' and uncomfortable. Hopefully in W5, the writers will not follow that route and address lupus like most books have done in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. I may be missing the difference between your post and mine. Are you saying some people find wolf-born werewolf on wolf also squicky? Because, sure, I can see that. As far as I'm aware, human and wolf kinfolk still can't interbreed.<br /> <br /> Hmm... I wonder if there are Garou sages pondering how there will never be a 'true' mix of wolf and man.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, it's weird how some W:tA books treat the concept as a big taboo. The first edition Book of the Wyrm, if memory serves, had a note about Homid Spirals taking pleasure in mating with Lupus kinfolk kept in cages\u2014frankly, I would not be surprised in the slightest if there are several packs or septs of Gaian Garou where the only difference is the size of the cage itself.<br /> <br /> Huh. It also says many Dancer Lupus kin are wolf-dogs. Meaning an influx of dog does not automatically kill the kinfolk spark. What are the Gaians doing that they can't expand their Lupus numbers that way? Last I checked, my homeland has 1300 wolves, and 9 MILLION DOGS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T13:02:12-07:00","id":1408773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408761#post1408761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um. I may be missing the difference between your post and mine. Are you saying some people find wolf-born werewolf on wolf also squicky? Because, sure, I can see that. As far as I'm aware, human and wolf kinfolk still can't interbreed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the very idea that lupus are a thing is an issue for these people. Often calling it dog r****.<br /> <br /> Funny enough, there are other books that treat the matter of lupus taking a human kin mate and homid taking a wolf-kin mate as fairly normal. Most of them do, in fact. So this is more of a recent/playerbase issue.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T13:02:31-07:00","id":1408774,"title":"","content":"Yeah my head cannon is that Lupus Garou especially in Urban areas, Mate with dogs, like there\u2019s this Bone Gnawers pack in my setting where a Lupus Bone Gnawer has a Stray dog as a mate, she\u2019s part of their pack, even if many other Garou disagree,<br /> <br /> Also book of the Wyld implies some Dog ancestry in Bone Gnawers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T13:25:02-07:00","id":1408782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408774#post1408774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah my head cannon is that Lupus Garou especially in Urban areas, Mate with dogs, like there\u2019s this Bone Gnawers pack in my setting where a Lupus Bone Gnawer has a Stray dog as a mate, she\u2019s part of their pack, even if many other Garou disagree,<br /> <br /> Also book of the Wyld implies some Dog ancestry in Bone Gnawers</div> </div> </div> </div>Any kind of implied dog ancestry would be with wolves, as it's kind of unavoidable at this point and is responsible for such traits as solid dark colored coats like the kind the Shadow Lords sport. The direct adoption of dogs as mates, though, is rather heavily contra Bone Gnawers as presented; a head canon far more distant than, say, a shameful secret kept among the Shadow Lords about their origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T14:19:36-07:00","id":1408787,"title":"","content":"Or just not treat Purebreed as the same thing as being a pure bred wild phenotype wolf, since high PB relates directly to how much a given Garou conforms to the fur patterns associated with their Tribe.<br /> <br /> The wolf-dog thing is, as has been touched on in the books, more a matter of spirit than biology anyway. It's purposefully left up to the ST on where to set the lines regarding how much &quot;wolf&quot; there needs to be to still have the spiritual connection of a kin, vs. how much domestication strips that connection away.<br /> <br /> Though I doubt Forsaken's choice to focus on just human born werewolves is going to make it into W5 anyway, and thus however individual tables feel about breeding, it's going to remain part of W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T14:27:28-07:00","id":1408789,"title":"","content":"Yeah they don\u2019t accept to have Garou children at least not in a generation, she\u2019s mostly their so the lupus can engage in \u201ccanid\u201d behavior she\u2019s also a very sweet girl who the Gnawers trained to do tricks like spotting vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T15:35:09-07:00","id":1408795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408773#post1408773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny enough, there are other books that treat the matter of lupus taking a human kin mate and homid taking a wolf-kin mate as fairly normal. Most of them do, in fact. So this is more of a recent/playerbase issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it must be a particular type of player. I've been running WtA for 25-ish years and its never come up as a point of issue in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T16:46:18-07:00","id":1408810,"title":"","content":"This was never a problem in the Werewolf game I played in, but tbh in this particular game we mostly handwaved the issue. The one lupus PC had a wolf Kinfolk mate, but he wasn\u2019t on screen that much. The other players stuck to romance with humans. Nobody had a problem with the idea of homid Garou mating with wolves, it just never came up. (Although we were kinda young at the time and it was a pretty short chronicle.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T17:57:55-07:00","id":1408818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408782#post1408782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any kind of implied dog ancestry would be with wolves, as it's kind of unavoidable at this point and is responsible for such traits as solid dark colored coats like the kind the Shadow Lords sport. The direct adoption of dogs as mates, though, is rather heavily contra Bone Gnawers as presented; a head canon far more distant than, say, a shameful secret kept among the Shadow Lords about their origins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why the Bone Gnawers specifically, if I may ask?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T19:08:14-07:00","id":1408826,"title":"","content":"The bone gnawers are not know for being selective about their breeding stock, they\u2019ll fuck just about anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T22:00:29-07:00","id":1408858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408818#post1408818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why the Bone Gnawers specifically, if I may ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a sore point that they have to refute more often than any other tribe.<br /> <br /> Edit: And is specifically called out in an ooc section of their revised tribe book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-18-2020, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T06:37:16-07:00","id":1408912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408795#post1408795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it must be a particular type of player. I've been running WtA for 25-ish years and its never come up as a point of issue in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen it crop up here and there, more recently. This is why I'm glad that Forsaken and Apocalypse exist concurrently, as there are those who want to play werewolves more like the mythical monster with murkier themes and do not like the more structured and species-like nature of the garou.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T09:45:49-07:00","id":1408957,"title":"","content":"I like Apocalypse better, but only cause I\u2019m more used to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T09:49:20-07:00","id":1408958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408858#post1408858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a sore point that they have to refute more often than any other tribe.<br /> <br /> Edit: And is specifically called out in an ooc section of their revised tribe book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaah! Thank you for clarifying!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:16:54-07:00","id":1409201,"title":"","content":"To answer to core point of this thread;<br /> <br /> I hope not, and not because I'm geared up to dislike W5. It is because we truly have found a good balance between Forsaken and Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Players who want to play Apocalypse want; Epic scale adventures, deep looks into environmentalism and biology, discussions of human rights, playing as non-humans, deep lore and fully realised setting, truly epic gory fights, tribal politics and werewolves as a species.<br /> <br /> <br /> Players who want to play Forsaken want; More typical werewolves, much vaguer and uncertain setting, no pre-made alliances/enemies between supernaturals, more freedom to create unique settings, no greater werewolf nation, smaller focus stories that are more personal, more flexible tribes and much more horror focused spirit world.<br /> <br /> I love both games a lot, but I love them for different reasons. In WtA, an ancient creature getting youtube famous would be a massive issue, but in WtF it is simply a hilarious factoid about a poor curious thing (Quattuor is adorable.)<br /> <br /> <br /> As I have said many times before, WtA -needs- its extensive lore to function and give the players the full WtA experience. WtF can be played with little use of its lore but the core basics.<br /> <br /> To make WtA like WtF, you lose a lot of what makes WtA so interesting. It is clunky, sure, but personally I love the clunk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:35:59-07:00","id":1409211,"title":"","content":"I agree that I would not want to see the core themes of WTA changed at all. Some stereotypes and derogatory things still need to be removed, some of the science about wolves and other animals needs updating, and the tribal weaknesses and Pure Breed fur patterns could use a total overhaul. But the core themes are the reason I love WTA, and a very cogent and pointed commentary on many of the most horrible problems caused by real world humans. WTF holds no attraction to me at all, except to mine for ideas to translate into WTA.<br /> <br /> I think perhaps the OP might have meant whether the mechanics of WTF should be used in W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T15:18:39-07:00","id":1409233,"title":"","content":"When other threads talked about the &quot;Requiem-ization of V5&quot; it was very much a mechanics focused thing (not that it didn't stray into setting as the two are linked and all).<br /> <br /> V5 didn't reduce the main Clans to 5 (though they made the questionable decision of only including the original 7 in the core book and left the expanded 6 for supplements despite multiple editions of them being considered core material). V5 didn't radically alter the VtM factions to be more like the Covenants (V5 still presents most cities as primarily one Sect, with some presence of one or two of the others, rather than VtR's more open Covenant dynamics). And so on.<br /> <br /> The discussion was things like the changed Attribute spreads, reduced variables in each roll (even if that's more like Storyteller Revised aka Trinity 1e), the inclusion of Touchstones, Blood Potency, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T18:46:48-07:00","id":1409263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1409211#post1409211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that I would not want to see the core themes of WTA changed at all. Some stereotypes and derogatory things still need to be removed, some of the science about wolves and other animals needs updating, and the tribal weaknesses and Pure Breed fur patterns could use a total overhaul. But the core themes are the reason I love WTA, and a very cogent and pointed commentary on many of the most horrible problems caused by real world humans. WTF holds no attraction to me at all, except to mine for ideas to translate into WTA.<br /> <br /> I think perhaps the OP might have meant whether the mechanics of WTF should be used in W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the Dinosaur shifters have to be changed know that people know that Dinosaurs where birds and not reptiles.<br /> <br /> Wolves don\u2019t have Omegas and Alphas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T22:00:45-07:00","id":1409292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1409263#post1409263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah the Dinosaur shifters have to be changed know that people know that Dinosaurs where birds and not reptiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on how you define clades, and also you have the Venn diagram relationship backward. All birds were dinosaurs, but not all dinosaurs were birds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wolves don\u2019t have Omegas and Alphas </div> </div> </div><u>Wild</u> wolves don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:22:04-07:00","id":1409392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1409292#post1409292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends on how you define clades, and also you have the Venn diagram relationship backward. All birds were dinosaurs, but not all dinosaurs were birds.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Dinosaurs <b>are</b> reptiles. Yes, birds are reptiles, in a cladistic sense.<br /> <br /> If Konradleijon meant reptiles in the cold-blooded, scaly, featherless sense, then dinosaurs and pterosaurs weren't reptiles. But most of them weren't birds either.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T13:24:16-07:00","id":1409411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1409201#post1409201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players who want to play Apocalypse want; Epic scale adventures, deep looks into environmentalism and biology, discussions of human rights, playing as non-humans, deep lore and fully realised setting, truly epic gory fights, tribal politics and werewolves as a species.<br /> <br /> Players who want to play Forsaken want; More typical werewolves, much vaguer and uncertain setting, no pre-made alliances/enemies between supernaturals, more freedom to create unique settings, no greater werewolf nation, smaller focus stories that are more personal, more flexible tribes and much more horror focused spirit world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we need to be careful when we say things like &quot;Players of X want this...&quot; because nobody is qualified to speak for the entire player base. You can only speak for yourself and your gaming groups. Not even this board as a whole speaks for the player base because we're not necessarily representative of the entire player base. For example, while I now post on these forums, I never posted on the old White Wolf forums.<br /> <br /> I say this because many of the things you've mentioned are not things I want or even particularly care for. I play Apocalypse, and don't play Forsaken. Yet I don't want epic scale adventures. I think the game too often seems like high fantasy rather than a world of earthly legends being true. I like things being more down to earth. I'm not sure what &quot;deep looks&quot; into environmentalism means. Yet even though I think some emphasis on protecting the wilderness is warranted, I think too much emphasis on environmental themes is bad for the game as it detracts from other things we can be doing in the setting. I'm not particularly interested in Captain Planet type games. I can't remember any discussion of human rights ever in any game I've been in, although there has certainly been moral dilemmas. Neither I nor my gaming buddies are particularly interested in playing non-humans (i.e. metis and lupus), although we're fine with it being an element in the setting. I do like much of the lore, tribal and sept politics, and the ability to expand the game into high drama in the umbra or Garou Nation when I want.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there are certainly things you mentioned about Forsaken that I do want in my Apocalypse games. I've never played Forsaken and have zero interest in it. But certainly there are some things I've hear about the setting that I've liked, and others that I have not.<br /> <br /> I think the game is improved when it gives tools to players and STs to run the style of game they want. I think the setting is large enough it can accommodate all sorts of things. Both the way you play, the way I play, and the way other plays. But I do think they need to give more options somewhere - in the corebook, ST guide, or other sourcebooks - to incorporate some of the Forsaken elements you mentioned (albeit fitting the Apocalypse setting) as well as other elements not mentioned here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T13:28:19-07:00","id":1409412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1409411#post1409411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we need to be careful when we say things like &quot;Players of X want this...&quot; because nobody is qualified to speak for the entire player base.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, I wasn't trying to say people want X, just that for me, those are things that make the settings different and potential deal breakers I've seen people have between settings.<br /> <br /> Apologies that it sounded likke I was speaking for others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T03:49:51-07:00","id":1410642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1409411#post1409411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we need to be careful when we say things like &amp;quot;Players of X want this...&amp;quot; because nobody is qualified to speak for the entire player base. You can only speak for yourself and your gaming groups. Not even this board as a whole speaks for the player base because we're not necessarily representative of the entire player base. For example, while I now post on these forums, I never posted on the old White Wolf forums.<br /> <br /> I say this because many of the things you've mentioned are not things I want or even particularly care for. I play Apocalypse, and don't play Forsaken. Yet I don't want epic scale adventures. I think the game too often seems like high fantasy rather than a world of earthly legends being true. I like things being more down to earth. I'm not sure what &amp;quot;deep looks&amp;quot; into environmentalism means. Yet even though I think some emphasis on protecting the wilderness is warranted, I think too much emphasis on environmental themes is bad for the game as it detracts from other things we can be doing in the setting. I'm not particularly interested in Captain Planet type games. I can't remember any discussion of human rights ever in any game I've been in, although there has certainly been moral dilemmas. Neither I nor my gaming buddies are particularly interested in playing non-humans (i.e. metis and lupus), although we're fine with it being an element in the setting. I do like much of the lore, tribal and sept politics, and the ability to expand the game into high drama in the umbra or Garou Nation when I want.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there are certainly things you mentioned about Forsaken that I do want in my Apocalypse games. I've never played Forsaken and have zero interest in it. But certainly there are some things I've hear about the setting that I've liked, and others that I have not.<br /> <br /> I think the game is improved when it gives tools to players and STs to run the style of game they want. I think the setting is large enough it can accommodate all sorts of things. Both the way you play, the way I play, and the way other plays. But I do think they need to give more options somewhere - in the corebook, ST guide, or other sourcebooks - to incorporate some of the Forsaken elements you mentioned (albeit fitting the Apocalypse setting) as well as other elements not mentioned here.</div> </div> </div> </div>About that their is a huge connection with Human right abuses and pollution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T09:27:17-07:00","id":1410696,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. Human rights abuses are a core part of industrial &quot;progress&quot;.<br /> <br /> Polluting factories, mine tailings, leaky pipelines, landfills, toxic waste, and nuclear waste are routinely put in communities of racially and/or economically oppressed people, so that the dominant groups don't have to suffer (or even hear about) the effects. It causes extreme health problems: congenital disabilities (&quot;birth defects&quot;), stillbirths, lots of nasty diseases, and now extra COVID vulnerability... plus the oil spills and chemical accidents also occur mostly in &quot;sacrifice zones&quot; inhabited by poor people and ethnic minorities. Those folks are also often living in the places most severely harmed by climate change, and most don't have the resources to move away. Then there's the &quot;man camps&quot; of non-Native men brought close to First Nation reservations to work pipelines and fracking rigs; some go raping and kidnapping Native American women in large numbers. And everywhere some tropical rainforest is being clearcut, there are disenfranchised native humans living there whose lives are being ruined as their homeland is stolen and literally destroyed.<br /> <br /> Even the people who end up taking health-destroying jobs in coal mines, refineries, chemical plants, and factory farms are in some cases folks who don't have many other job options, especially in rural communities with collapsing economies - so they're also being exploited in a way. When the local fossil fuels or metals run out, companies sometimes just take all the money and abandon them (leaving the toxic waste behind).<br /> <br /> If the people who profit and benefit the most from cheap fossil fuels and chemical products had to live with the pollution dumped in their own backyards and killing their own families, they might be less willing to keep using the stuff.<br /> <br /> In WTA there's the added horror of banes coming to roost and breed in all these gutted industrial hellscapes and screwing around with the angry, desperate locals. And hey! when they're really desperate and despairing, not only are they more vulnerable to possession, but it's easier to tempt them to do more and more heinous things for the Wyrm, in return for medicine or jobs or money or food ... hey, Pentex has all those things!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  trying to reduce rantingness 08-27-2020, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T11:23:05-07:00","id":1410718,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean to go on a rant, sorry. To bring this more to &quot;what could W5 look like&quot; this question of human suffering could be a point of contention between tribes. I imagine many Garou really don't worry much about the suffering of non-Kinfolk humans. Bone Gnawers, Uktena, Wendigo, and maybe Children of Gaia could be trying to convince the other Garou this is something they should care about. On the other side of the debate, many Garou might say well, that's sad, but we have more important things to fight - not realizing that human suffering feeds the Wyrm. And of course the Red Talons would say They're human, collective guilt, they deserve it and they &quot;allow&quot; it to happen. But of course it would be boring if every werewolf followed the 'expected' attitude of their tribe or breed.<br /> <br /> This is also something that could be a huge point of argument among Fera in poor, developing countries. On the one hand, how do you save forests and savannahs and wildlife, except stopping (killing?) the people who cut and plow and shoot and drill and mine? But must environmental protection come at the expense of poverty? Is poverty better than pollution? Poverty often drives people to cut trees and shoot wildlife and exhaust the soil, just to bring firewood and food to their families. If they can't get jobs working in a polluting industry, they either have to move to the scabs, or they turn to killing the land. Do you restart the Impergium... and make the locals really hate and fear the wild and the animals? Do you try to encourage ecotourism and all the tourists (and who knows what...) they may bring? What the heck do you do about population growth? What do you do about poaching, if the demand for parts is coming from another country altogether? Different Fera species live in different habitats, so you may even get shifters who want to protect <i>their</i> animal's land, even if that means the farmers go slash-and-burn somebody else's animal's habitat. Do the forest shifters get in fights with the grassland or wetland shifters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T19:06:57-07:00","id":1410792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1410696#post1410696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. Human rights abuses are a core part of industrial &amp;quot;progress&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Polluting factories, mine tailings, leaky pipelines, landfills, toxic waste, and nuclear waste are routinely put in communities of racially and/or economically oppressed people, so that the dominant groups don't have to suffer (or even hear about) the effects. It causes extreme health problems: congenital disabilities (&amp;quot;birth defects&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, stillbirths, lots of nasty diseases, and now extra COVID vulnerability... plus the oil spills and chemical accidents also occur mostly in &amp;quot;sacrifice zones&amp;quot; inhabited by poor people and ethnic minorities. Those folks are also often living in the places most severely harmed by climate change, and most don't have the resources to move away. Then there's the &amp;quot;man camps&amp;quot; of non-Native men brought close to First Nation reservations to work pipelines and fracking rigs; some go raping and kidnapping Native American women in large numbers. And everywhere some tropical rainforest is being clearcut, there are disenfranchised native humans living there whose lives are being ruined as their homeland is stolen and literally destroyed.<br /> <br /> Even the people who end up taking health-destroying jobs in coal mines, refineries, chemical plants, and factory farms are in some cases folks who don't have many other job options, especially in rural communities with collapsing economies - so they're also being exploited in a way. When the local fossil fuels or metals run out, companies sometimes just take all the money and abandon them (leaving the toxic waste behind).<br /> <br /> If the people who profit and benefit the most from cheap fossil fuels and chemical products had to live with the pollution dumped in their own backyards and killing their own families, they might be less willing to keep using the stuff.<br /> <br /> In WTA there's the added horror of banes coming to roost and breed in all these gutted industrial hellscapes and screwing around with the angry, desperate locals. And hey! when they're really desperate and despairing, not only are they more vulnerable to possession, but it's easier to tempt them to do more and more heinous things for the Wyrm, in return for medicine or jobs or money or food ... hey, Pentex has all those things!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah what most Garou don\u2019t know is that the Exploitation of people and the environment are hugely interconnected,<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2020/jul/28/climate-change-enviromental-racism-america\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/24134ce7acc48767f467f1bb5aa2f81ce4190b90/0_126_3781_2269/master/3781.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;quality=85&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;precrop=40:21,offset-x50,offset-y0&amp;overlay-align=bottom%2Cleft&amp;overlay-width=100p&amp;overlay-base64=L2ltZy9zdGF0aWMvb3ZlcmxheXMvdGctb3BpbmlvbnMtYWdlLTIwMjAucG5n&amp;enable=upscale&amp;s=e88e951a648d37bc3b216b5d1afd125b\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2020/jul/28/climate-change-enviromental-racism-america\" target=\"_blank\"> Environmental racism is killing Americans of color. Climate change will make it worse | Mustafa Santiago Ali </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2020/jul/28/climate-change-enviromental-racism-america\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2020/jul/28/climate-change-enviromental-racism-america </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> We&rsquo;ve turned a blind eye to a public health time bomb in already vulnerable communities </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T18:37:19-08:00","id":1432989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1407817#post1407817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You're running the edge on Edition warring. It may not be your cup of tea but some people love Forsaken.</span><br /> <br /> Mind you, I'm heavily biased.<br /> <br /> I actually did my longest Werewolf: The Apocalypse game adapting Werewolf: The Forsaken. The premise was Albretch noticed that the spirit of the Great Wolf was insane and the cause of so much of the werewolf races' misery. The Beast of War had corrupted it long ago and that was the reason why all werewolves suffered frenzies and the War of Rage against other races as well as the Impergium. So, Albretch killed it and all werewolves felt the affects.<br /> <br /> However, it resulted in a Civil War as the fundamentalist psychotic Garou that we know and loathe went to form the Pure while Albretch and company's followers became known as the Forsaken because Luna was PISSED by this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a record of this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T19:20:23-08:00","id":1432996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1410696#post1410696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then there's the &amp;quot;man camps&amp;quot; of non-Native men brought close to First Nation reservations to work pipelines and fracking rigs; some go raping and kidnapping Native American women in large numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a source on this?<br /> Edit: Nervermind, I found it: <a href=\"https://www.dailykos.com/stories/2018/9/23/1798048/-It-s-Legal-to-Rape-Native-American-Women-in-America\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dailykos.com/stories/201...men-in-America</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.dailykos.com/stories/2008/8/19/570016/-\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dailykos.com/stories/2008/8/19/570016/-</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.dailykos.com/stories/2019/2/7/1833163/-Why-Are-So-Many-Native-American-Women-Abused-Missing-and-Murdered\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dailykos.com/stories/201...g-and-Murdered</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.dailykos.com/stories/2019/12/21/1907207/-Saturday-snippets-Cops-ignored-rapes-of-Native-women-no-lying-about-Afghan-war-claims-top-general\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dailykos.com/stories/201...ms-top-general</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.dailykos.com/stories/2013/1/4/1176397/-Stop-Cover-Up-of-Lakota-Child-Rape-in-South-Dakota\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dailykos.com/stories/201...n-South-Dakota</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","user":"ryu238","date":". 01-22-2021, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T02:38:36-08:00","id":1433150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1432989#post1432989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have a record of this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope but I can go into more detail if you like. It was a fun reorganization of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T12:21:50-08:00","id":1433171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433150#post1433150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope but I can go into more detail if you like. It was a fun reorganization of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes please! <br /> <br /> I remember this fun little in-character discussions between characters from both versions of the WoD and came across this: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/n-owod-in-character-crossover-discussions.392895/post-9836353\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...5/post-9836353</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You just don't seem to get it, do you? This is basically how the spirit world would work anyway. It's an ecosystem, just like the one in the material world. It's built off a few simple principles (spirits get essence from encouraging the thing they represent or by consuming other spirits), and it is an emergent result of those rules. It's an ecosystem where everything is autotrophic, but can also be heterotrophic, and can get more energy that way. And game theory combined with evolutionary biology (modified using &quot;The Precepts of Essentophagia&quot;) predicts accurately what will form to fill those niches<br /> <br /> Spirits are really very simple beings. Even the most intelligent are less rounded, less balanced than a seven year old child. For them, the thing they represent is life, so they encourage it. For a human, that is horrific, but objectively it is rational, although in many cases short sighted due to the damage that they do to the natural world, lacking as they do to look beyond their concepts or objects.<br /> <br /> Now, your hisil is the mess, and it's obviously artificial. Why are all those spirits cooperating? What's their incentive? The only time the Other gets so organised is when a larger being is artificially enforcing their personal laws on it, like what you get around a Wound. All your Gaia seems to be is a larger version of one of the Malejin... that's our Malejin, not yours, and even our ones are natural evolutions of the predominance of vice in human nature. Anyway, yes, your Gaia seems to just control the Spirit world, shaping it in Its vision, and if there's two things I've learned, it's that Spirits are ultimately alien in the way that they think (although very simple once you get into that mindset), and that they never have the best interests in mankind at heart. </div> </div> </div>And this: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/n-owod-in-character-crossover-discussions.392895/post-17367670\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre.../post-17367670</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the Weaver is order, the Wyld is chaos and the Wyrm is destruction. You go through controlled changes and are intent on killing just about everyone and everything through use of your rage at, well, almost everything? But somehow you don't see that the Wyld is no stronger in you than the Weaver and you don't see yourselves as children of the Wyrm? Although I do have to grant that having such delusions does indicate that maybe the Wyld is slightly stronger in you than the Weaver. </div> </div> </div>And especially thirealizations came up as well.<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/n-owod-in-character-crossover-discussions.392895/post-9836276\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...5/post-9836276</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll observe that the same question applies to you guys, given that the major source of your information comes from your spiritual masters, who wouldn't at all have a vested interest in keeping you fearful and worried about impending doom rather than about who's pulling your strings. But hey, I guess a collection of terrible ethnic stereotypes with a genocidal past wouldn't really want to examine themselves that closely anyhow... -- Rhiannon Davies of the Iron Masters, who was driven to drink by the bloody Fianna, and is being somewhat bitter while consuming bitter </div> </div> </div>Please tell me if these realizations came up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T21:46:40-08:00","id":1433358,"title":"","content":"This thread was a wild ride for sure. But answering the question at hand:<br /> No, I don't think it will be Forsaken reskinned. Just as V5 isn't Re-Requiem. And well, Masquerade and Requiem are (in my opinion) closer to each other than Apocalypse and Forsaken, and so they will be even more different.<br /> <br /> To let things clear. I fuching love Forsaken, I like the themes, the mythos, mechanics, politics, distribution, handling of what a &quot;vanilla&quot; setting would be, more urban and territory based chronicles, more use of the original werewolf legends and et cetera. But, I really like the potential of Apocalypse and many of its ideas. Warriors and sages that are burned by their own passion and struggle to keep or change things? That's cool. A megacorp that embodies what is wrong with the &quot;system&quot; and acts as The Man to be opposed, questioned, manipulated, or swayed by? Awesome. Internal struggles, intrigues and ideological discussion? Nice, but I do think it's kinda... &quot;you have to take part in this predetermined setting of goals, foes and friends&quot; which for me takes away from the egocentrism of WoD games; vampires do their shtick to survive and go on, werewolves seem to war the wyrm and weaver just because they &quot;should&quot; and everyone seem just to be &quot;okay, I'l fight&quot; and go from there. Of course, it depends on how each one reads the setting but for me it's a bit too much pre-defined as to what you do and don't, it lacks a bit of nuance for my liking. The Forsaken seem to do what they do because it benefits them, and they feel what is too ignore their natures or &quot;duty&quot; quite quickly and close to home, spirits and other shapeshifters running rampant or being made run rampant by the action of humans (or other supernatural) is really bad news. Besides, they are gangs taking care of their territory (or hunting grounds), as predators (at least) thematically do. So all and all I would like 70-80% Apocalypse and 20% Forsaken on W5, but I probably will end up adapting W5 to resemble Forsaken a bit more either way.<br /> The Wyrm and Weaver shouldn't be &quot;ow the mad and cruel faces of evil&quot;, but something that by the actions of humans have been unbalanced (and yes that's pretty much what happened, but it mostly seems to be just the crazy evil and strict evil powers that hurt the green-greens and must be stopped). There should be more leeway to calm them down and return to balance rather then obliterate them or their lackeys. I think the whole &quot;Apocalypse is coming&quot; hurts this possibility, and maybe something as V5 does that &quot;Gehenna is cyclical&quot; and is a period rather than a single event would benefit the setting immensely. I mean, we are at Apocalypses, people are dying for profit, world politics are looking like a shithouse, huge forests and biomes are being burned by negligence, viruses and diseases are being bred from this natural chaos, the world is being drained by a thick straw. It is up to the Werewolves to keep what's left, try to reverse the other side (because raging and throwing yourself at them makes them win the war), try to guide humanity (or go Red Talons at them and pay the price), and bring back balance to this spiritual and wordily mess, mostly because they can see right at their face (spirits) coming out of all this dump, and affecting or hurting the people around them. They need to stop it because they might be able to, and if they don't, they and their loved ones will suffer. For me, that would be epic battle of Werewolf The Apocalypse 5th edition, a changing world that in-fighting and negligence will only leave it as the falling snowball that it is, which is (or will eventually) hurting you and the people around you directly (since you see the spirits coming from it).<br /> When will you rage? More like, should you? Or, at who and how. The Garou must be build, rebalance, not only destroy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T00:08:45-08:00","id":1433776,"title":"","content":"Apocalypse and Forsaken are very different games trying to do very different things. I really hope they don't mess up W5 but seeing how V5 was done I don't have much of a flicker of hope.<br /> <br /> My general hopes:<br /> <br /> 1) Don't remove the Umbra (because if they do, all bets are off for hope any of the other lines are good)<br /> <br /> 2) DON'T add Touchstones (its stupid that even Forsaken has Touchstones aswell, I thought only Requiem had that... just, why? why??)<br /> <br /> 3) Come up with original overhauls; i.e not just blindly ripping stuff from VtR like VTM did. Actually oWoD mechanics were fine, the only problem was that combat was too slow. They should revise something to make it more faster.<br /> <br /> 4) Don't incorporate CofD Attributes (they are horrible compared to oWoD)<br /> <br /> 5) Get the Weaver and Wlyd to finally get their own books like the Wyrm has had. I think the Weaver may have got atleast one(?) book before, but not the Wlyd... AT ALL. Such a force of primordial chaos is such a shame that it didn't get more work put into it. Also with the Wlyd being heavily aspected to nature and most W:tA (realistically from an IC standpoint) should be rural areas (not urban ones) how come the Wlyd wasn't broached on more before?<br /> <br /> 6) DON'T make the Umbra harder to access. Make the Umbra more important to the setting more than it was. <br /> <br /> 7) Make the Weaver a more prominent antagonist along with the Wyrm. I always found it odd that the Garou barely even hunted or tried to investigate the Weaver since it along WITH the Wyrm (despite being enemies) is responsible for humanities unrestrained growth and influence in destroying the natural environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T04:15:29-08:00","id":1433785,"title":"","content":"There is a Book of the Wyld but it\u2019s not that good IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T04:23:02-08:00","id":1433786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433776#post1433776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) DON'T add Touchstones (its stupid that even Forsaken has Touchstones aswell, I thought only Requiem had that... just, why? why??)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, even more importantly because Touchstones being in V5 doesn't bode well for them being only in V5, it's really important for the 5e games to actually pay attention to how the different CofD games alter how Touchstones work in the different CofD 2e games that use them (some do, some don't, and the ones that do frequently do in very different ways).<br /> <br /> VtR Touchstones are a bulwark against Humanity loss, ideally you want a few, and for them to not be in conflict with each other to create a stable emotional base for your vampire; they also help vampires regain WP when VtR vampires don't during the day sleep.<br /> <br /> WtF Touchstones help werewolves keep their Harmony where it is. If you're balanced, that's generally a good thing. That's why you only get two, and they're in opposition to each other. One that pulls you towards your spirit half, and one towards your flesh half. If you feel yourself slipping in one direction, your Touchstone of the opposite can be a way to pull you back to the middle. However, imbalance towards either extreme come with a lot of potential benefits for certain situations. Touchstones here serve the purpose of also making it a more significant and time consuming choice to push yourself to an extreme; esp. since they can make it harder to get back since you probably snubbed one in favor of the other in the process.<br /> <br /> Whether you like the idea of Touchstones or not, or V5's version or not, a bigger mistake than adding them to W5 is to add V5's specific version of them to W5 and make them disconnected from the concerns of werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) Get the Weaver and Wlyd to finally get their own books like the Wyrm has had. I think the Weaver may have got atleast one(?) book before, but not the Wlyd... AT ALL. </div> </div> </div>All three of the Triat got a book in Revised:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3369\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/3369.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3369\" target=\"_blank\"> Book of the Wyld - White Wolf | Werewolf: The Apocalypse Revised | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3369\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3369 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Book of the Wyld - Primal Chaos The Weaver has tried to bind it. The Wyrm has tried to devour it. It's beset on all sides, it's back to the </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Though any significant change to the Umbra should still mean there should be a focus on addressing these topics right away (though, really, a single &quot;Book of the Triat&quot; could be done as more supplements are longer books now than the shorter ones during the oWW treadmill days; much like V20 did a single book for all the Clans instead of 13 smaller Clanbooks).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) DON'T make the Umbra harder to access. Make the Umbra more important to the setting more than it was. </div> </div> </div>These should probably be treated as two separate points.<br /> <br /> While the Umbra doesn't necessarily need to be harder or easier to access in general, it could use an overhaul so when it's easy and when it's hard fight the narratives a bit better.<br /> <br /> The importance of the Umbra in direct play should probably stay a table focus decision. Not every group is going to want to have to spend lots of time in the Umbra, others are going to want to spend as much time as they can justify there. The current lore of the game gives Garou lots of reasons to care about the Umbra and spend time there... I'm not sure it really needs more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-29-2021, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T19:38:36-08:00","id":1433871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433785#post1433785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Book of the Wyld but it\u2019s not that good IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was unpolished, perhaps, and the ST section could have been more directed, but the concepts that it introduced were interesting, and the raw feeling of it helped in some places. It's also one of the few books published post-core that presents the Triat as possibly being greater than Gaia, though for some reason, few people who are quick to bring that seldom-used alternative up seek to cite the Wyldbook as a source for anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T22:00:54-08:00","id":1433883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Triat as possibly being greater than Gaia,</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I definitely have to get that book!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T01:24:20-08:00","id":1433896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433871#post1433871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was unpolished, perhaps, and the ST section could have been more directed, but the concepts that it introduced were interesting, and the raw feeling of it helped in some places. It's also one of the few books published post-core that presents the Triat as possibly being greater than Gaia, though for some reason, few people who are quick to bring that seldom-used alternative up seek to cite the Wyldbook as a source for anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Triat and Gaia are coequal. Like a Quadrat. But that\u2019s just me.<br /> <br /> Crying rn. Not you just random emotions using this discussion to distract myself and not entirely working. I only mention it cause some small ironic part of my brain thinks this may be the only time in history someone has actually cried while talking about whether the Triat is greater than Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T03:01:28-08:00","id":1433902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433896#post1433896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Triat and Gaia are coequal. Like a Quadrat. But that\u2019s just me.<br /> <br /> Crying rn. Not you just random emotions using this discussion to distract myself and not entirely working. I only mention it cause some small ironic part of my brain thinks this may be the only time in history someone has actually cried while talking about whether the Triat is greater than Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>To whoever Liked this post: if you\u2019re who I think you are, I miss you and I\u2019m sorry. If you\u2019re not, thanks for the Like anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T21:10:12-08:00","id":1433980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433786#post1433786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, even more importantly because Touchstones being in V5 doesn't bode well for them being only in V5, it's really important for the 5e games to actually pay attention to how the different CofD games alter how Touchstones work in the different CofD 2e games that use them (some do, some don't, and the ones that do frequently do in very different ways).<br /> <br /> VtR Touchstones are a bulwark against Humanity loss, ideally you want a few, and for them to not be in conflict with each other to create a stable emotional base for your vampire; they also help vampires regain WP when VtR vampires don't during the day sleep.<br /> <br /> WtF Touchstones help werewolves keep their Harmony where it is. If you're balanced, that's generally a good thing. That's why you only get two, and they're in opposition to each other. One that pulls you towards your spirit half, and one towards your flesh half. If you feel yourself slipping in one direction, your Touchstone of the opposite can be a way to pull you back to the middle. However, imbalance towards either extreme come with a lot of potential benefits for certain situations. Touchstones here serve the purpose of also making it a more significant and time consuming choice to push yourself to an extreme; esp. since they can make it harder to get back since you probably snubbed one in favor of the other in the process.<br /> <br /> Whether you like the idea of Touchstones or not, or V5's version or not, a bigger mistake than adding them to W5 is to add V5's specific version of them to W5 and make them disconnected from the concerns of werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that people that play Werewolf are many times the same people who don't like the Humanity mechanics and all that struggle, or at the very least they think it should stay in Vampire, but stay away from Werewolf. I agree that each game should feel distinct, but goddamit, it still is World of Darkness. If you are just a strong guy doing strong things against evil doers with no people to care or balance to make it takes away from the themes. So I can see some Harmony mechanic, with Touchstone or what have you acting as the wordly, human side of the Werewolf. Because... Rage, Gifts, dealing with spirits, turning lupus and crinos, sticking with your pack, and all that, it is already pretty heavy on the spirit side. Something I really liked of Chronicles of Darkness (that V5 took it) was that Power, always came with a cost (Blood Potency bringing Feed limitations and Bane Severity), Forsaken had it too. The old world of darkness usually just made a vertical scale, that the higher the better no questions about it. So, there is no reason, but Humanity (that was negligible, or you could just follow a Path of Enlightenment) and maybe a few story beats, not to Diablerie your way to power; now you can and it's cool but there is heavier a price (hell, even if players start at higher BP there is hell to pay). And I hope Harmony and the Gnosis (or some better name) stick to this ethos. I mean, you will Rage, but, should you? And can you take it all? A powerful werewolf should be detached from humans, and end up using its power against the Weaver or Wyrm and end it all in a blaze of glory for it has nowhere to employ it.<br /> <br /> Now, Umbra is cool and all, I don't like it much. Spelljammer and Planescape has that stuff already, and it isn't much of a World of Darkness if you are &quot;outside&quot; the World of Darkness. Now, the close Umbra and the reflex of our world, that is cool, spirits are rampant and you can either dominate or destroy them, or find out what is happening on the real world that is causing all this spiritual ruckus. That is cool, and one of the highest points of Werewolf. <br /> Problem is, V5 is very conservative with its metaplot, with its info about the &quot;other&quot; worlds of darkness (the other splats), and is also showing to be more mundane, less esoteric, whimsical or explosive. For me it doesn't take away, it enhances, it brings closer to home, it feels weighty and dramatic. But I wonder what will happen with the more outworldly splats of WoD. With the format of V5, for example, I can't imagine a text about Umbra you know? So I think W5 will already have a tone shift from V5 just cuz of the tones, themes and cosmos of Werewolf. And I wonder how the Storyteller 5th edition paradigm will be in Werewolf. Will they tone it down? Will it be just like before, if only a bit more subtle and local? Will W5 adapt to the 5th edition or will 5th edition adapt to Werewolf? is what I'm asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T02:55:33-08:00","id":1434000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433980#post1433980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see that people that play Werewolf are many times the same people who don't like the Humanity mechanics and all that struggle, or at the very least they think it should stay in Vampire, but stay away from Werewolf. I agree that each game should feel distinct, but goddamit, it still is World of Darkness. If you are just a strong guy doing strong things against evil doers with no people to care or balance to make it takes away from the themes. So I can see some Harmony mechanic, with Touchstone or what have you acting as the wordly, human side of the Werewolf. Because... Rage, Gifts, dealing with spirits, turning lupus and crinos, sticking with your pack, and all that, it is already pretty heavy on the spirit side. Something I really liked of Chronicles of Darkness (that V5 took it) was that Power, always came with a cost (Blood Potency bringing Feed limitations and Bane Severity), Forsaken had it too. The old world of darkness usually just made a vertical scale, that the higher the better no questions about it. So, there is no reason, but Humanity (that was negligible, or you could just follow a Path of Enlightenment) and maybe a few story beats, not to Diablerie your way to power; now you can and it's cool but there is heavier a price (hell, even if players start at higher BP there is hell to pay). And I hope Harmony and the Gnosis (or some better name) stick to this ethos. I mean, you will Rage, but, should you? And can you take it all? A powerful werewolf should be detached from humans, and end up using its power against the Weaver or Wyrm and end it all in a blaze of glory for it has nowhere to employ it.<br /> <br /> Now, Umbra is cool and all, I don't like it much. Spelljammer and Planescape has that stuff already, and it isn't much of a World of Darkness if you are &quot;outside&quot; the World of Darkness. Now, the close Umbra and the reflex of our world, that is cool, spirits are rampant and you can either dominate or destroy them, or find out what is happening on the real world that is causing all this spiritual ruckus. That is cool, and one of the highest points of Werewolf.<br /> Problem is, V5 is very conservative with its metaplot, with its info about the &quot;other&quot; worlds of darkness (the other splats), and is also showing to be more mundane, less esoteric, whimsical or explosive. For me it doesn't take away, it enhances, it brings closer to home, it feels weighty and dramatic. But I wonder what will happen with the more outworldly splats of WoD. With the format of V5, for example, I can't imagine a text about Umbra you know? So I think W5 will already have a tone shift from V5 just cuz of the tones, themes and cosmos of Werewolf. And I wonder how the Storyteller 5th edition paradigm will be in Werewolf. Will they tone it down? Will it be just like before, if only a bit more subtle and local? Will W5 adapt to the 5th edition or will 5th edition adapt to Werewolf? is what I'm asking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok..........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T19:40:00-08:00","id":1434071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433980#post1433980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see that people that play Werewolf are many times the same people who don't like the Humanity mechanics and all that struggle, or at the very least they think it should stay in Vampire, but stay away from Werewolf. I agree that each game should feel distinct, but goddamit, it still is World of Darkness. If you are just a strong guy doing strong things against evil doers with no people to care or balance to make it takes away from the themes. So I can see some Harmony mechanic, with Touchstone or what have you acting as the wordly, human side of the Werewolf. Because... Rage, Gifts, dealing with spirits, turning lupus and crinos, sticking with your pack, and all that, it is already pretty heavy on the spirit side. Something I really liked of Chronicles of Darkness (that V5 took it) was that Power, always came with a cost (Blood Potency bringing Feed limitations and Bane Severity), Forsaken had it too. The old world of darkness usually just made a vertical scale, that the higher the better no questions about it. So, there is no reason, but Humanity (that was negligible, or you could just follow a Path of Enlightenment) and maybe a few story beats, not to Diablerie your way to power; now you can and it's cool but there is heavier a price (hell, even if players start at higher BP there is hell to pay). And I hope Harmony and the Gnosis (or some better name) stick to this ethos. I mean, you will Rage, but, should you? And can you take it all? A powerful werewolf should be detached from humans, and end up using its power against the Weaver or Wyrm and end it all in a blaze of glory for it has nowhere to employ it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage already always had a cost, and it was also possible to lose it, so no change necessary, there (well, maybe to dial back the concept of Thrall of the Wyrm, which didn't quite exist in 1e). Gnosis has its price in the time and effort required to maintain it (nowhere near as easy as just knocking over a human and draining their blood). Most of what's frightening about being a werewolf involves doing things that people relate to, but to frightening levels, so there's no reason for them to be out of touch like with low Humanity vampires, either. When they get hit hard and heal back, it hurts, and they can get some serious lasting scars from it as reminders of their mortality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, Umbra is cool and all, I don't like it much. Spelljammer and Planescape has that stuff already, and it isn't much of a World of Darkness if you are &quot;outside&quot; the World of Darkness. Now, the close Umbra and the reflex of our world, that is cool, spirits are rampant and you can either dominate or destroy them, or find out what is happening on the real world that is causing all this spiritual ruckus. That is cool, and one of the highest points of Werewolf.<br /> Problem is, V5 is very conservative with its metaplot, with its info about the &quot;other&quot; worlds of darkness (the other splats), and is also showing to be more mundane, less esoteric, whimsical or explosive. For me it doesn't take away, it enhances, it brings closer to home, it feels weighty and dramatic. But I wonder what will happen with the more outworldly splats of WoD. With the format of V5, for example, I can't imagine a text about Umbra you know? So I think W5 will already have a tone shift from V5 just cuz of the tones, themes and cosmos of Werewolf. And I wonder how the Storyteller 5th edition paradigm will be in Werewolf. Will they tone it down? Will it be just like before, if only a bit more subtle and local? Will W5 adapt to the 5th edition or will 5th edition adapt to Werewolf? is what I'm asking. </div> </div> </div>Vampire is an unreliable narrator here. Its focus monsters are spiritually deadened and view any with the capacity to delve into those matters with side-eye (Malkavains and Heketa are not exactly the pillars of their society). Given how numb and ignorant Vampire is to this corner, there's no reason that V5 should limit the totality of what fits into the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T18:06:38-08:00","id":1435129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433871#post1433871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was unpolished, perhaps, and the ST section could have been more directed, but the concepts that it introduced were interesting, and the raw feeling of it helped in some places. It's also one of the few books published post-core that presents the Triat as possibly being greater than Gaia, though for some reason, few people who are quick to bring that seldom-used alternative up seek to cite the Wyldbook as a source for anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here is a pretty good capsule review of the whole book. I've really enjoyed it, even if the writers had some awesome ideas and some times were just tossing &quot;oh just do something random&quot; at a chapter. In general the Weaver and Wyld books were formative of my view of Werewolf and it's Cosmology. Wyrm less so, because it was already pretty clear what it was and what it wanted in other books.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T18:08:07-08:00","id":1435131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433883#post1433883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now I definitely have to get that book!</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to look into the Ananasi book as well for a really interesting interpretation of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T10:26:21-08:00","id":1437973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1433150#post1433150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope but I can go into more detail if you like. It was a fun reorganization of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dude you there? I wish to hear how you handled this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T16:04:48-08:00","id":1438038,"title":"","content":"If the Umbra is cut off, then I'll have zero interest in W5. It is a huge, huge part of what makes Werewolf the game that it is. In every previous edition, how much you use the Umbra is a decision made at the table, not a possibility controlled by the content of the books. If someone doesn't want to use it at their table, they can. If the books make it impossible and then change the mechanics so that the old Umbra books are incompatible with the new rules, then that takes away everyone's choice about how to use the Umbra and forces the developer's decisions down their throat. This was a colossal wedge in the Mage community when they forced it on Mage, and it'll be just as big a mistake when they force it on Werewolf.<br /> <br /> I also see no reason for a Humanity mechanic. Shapeshifters are not human, and they're not <b>supposed</b> to be human. They are not cursed ex-humans struggling to maintain the shreds of their human nature and not to become monsters. Shapeshifters were created to be exactly and precisely what they are, by a vast divine being who is literally the world. Their internal struggle is to avoid falling to the Wyrm, and more broadly to avoid unnecessarily killing people. This is about character development, not a number. It should not become a number because it's far, far more complicated than % Humanity vs. % werewolfness. Shapeshifters can fall the Wyrm, the Weaver, the Wyld, or just Rage itself. They can become horrific and inhuman without departing at all from their divinely ordained purpose in the universe, because they are inherently inhuman. It's also entirely in-theme to play a game all about the external struggle against Wyrm monsters, and not worry about the internal struggle (especially on battlefields far away from human populations).<br /> <br /> Adding a Humanity mechanic to Werewolf would just unnecessarily shoehorn a Vampire theme into a completely different game where it doesn't belong. There is no reason whatsoever to add it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-04-2021, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T16:45:25-08:00","id":1438045,"title":"","content":"Rage has been the Humanity of Werewolf. You generally need to have it in order to engage in the game as it was intended (having none means you're at or near Losing the Beast and being unable to shapeshift, possibly marking a character getting retired), and having more of it makes the characters feel more - not that this is necessarily a pleasant prospect when you're going up against what most Garou and Fera are facing.<br /> <br /> (Nuwisha and Ananasi are like Werewolf's Paths of Enlightenment and KotE, respectively. The former follows a spiritual path dictated by a mandatory personal totem to focus on acting in the world, while the latter is more like the play style of another game dropped into the mix)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T02:25:09-08:00","id":1438090,"title":"","content":"I feel that a lot of these complaints people had towards &quot;no humanity in Werewolf and Mage&quot; came from people doing way too much crossover and not actually focusing on what Mage and Werewolf were about, and how things were set up. Both games created a lot of drama and character growth that questioned many moral and philisophical values and created depth and responsibility on their own terms without a trait like Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T03:01:52-08:00","id":1438093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1437973#post1437973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude you there? I wish to hear how you handled this.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>My Werewolf: The Forsaken/Apocalypse Campaign</b><br /> <br /> Essentially the idea was that the Apocalypse was prepared and off to a good start in 2004 with the Spirit World having the Red Star as well as the Wyrm overflowing with Power. That was when King Albretch had a vision (supposedly) sent to him from Phoenix that there was a corruption in the heart of the Garou Nation that had been there for millennia. It was the source of the Wyrm being able to influence them to the Impergium, The War of Rage, and so many other horrifyingly STUPID decisions that they'd made over the years.<br /> <br /> <b>The Great Wolf</b>, a Totem that the Garou had forgotten even existed and all other Wolf Totems were a shade of like Fenris or the Old Wolf of the Woods had been corrupted by the Beast of War long ago. Albretch had a choice between either trying to redeem the Great Wolf or kill him in order to cancel the Apocalypse as it was his madness that was going to drive the Garou to all commit collective suicide by going into the Umbra for a thoroughly unnecessary glorious &quot;Ragnarok&quot;-style end.<br /> <br /> Evan Heals the Past (A Child of Gaia in my game after being rejected by the Wendigo for obvious damn reasons) argues the former but unsurprisingly, albeit perhaps disappointingly, Albretch heads with the Silver Pack to kill the Great Wolf in a strange vision quest. Possessed by an unknown spirit, Albretch and company kill the Great Wolf and the apocalypse is seemingly averted. The Red Star disappears and the Wyrm retreats. It also <i>pisses Luna off</i>. All Garou can feel her rage over what has been done and it's assumed by some that Albretch royally fucked up and others that he made a harsh but necessary call.<br /> <br /> Albretch being assassinated by someone is pretty much inevitable and happens but what follows is worse. The Garou Nation had actually been fracturing for centuries and this was the straw that broke the camel's back. Both agreed the Garou Nation had to change but two utterly incompatible visions for that emerged from the conflict.<br /> <br /> <b>The Pure</b>: A group consisting of mostly Get of Fenris, Silver Fangs, Red Talons, Wendigo, and stragglers from other tribes forms around a &quot;Return to our Roots&quot; ethos that believes the Garou need to undermine modern civilization, slaughter whoever disagrees with them, and keep the bloodlines pure. They also want to cull the Garou Nation of those who have lost their way by being too close to Homid society, befriending Fera, or being &quot;impure.&quot; It starts as a minority group but gradually grows as Luna seems to bless their actions as well as give them Gifts to kill other Garou, find new Garou faster, and breed truer.<br /> <br /> <b>The Forsaken</b>: The group consisting of everyone else but primarily the Children of Gaia, Shadow Lords, Bone Gnawers, Uktena, and Glass Walkers. They have a belief that the old ways were broken and they needed to adapt to the Modern World as well as cast aside the old mistakes. They would be guardians of mortals against the Wyrms and their territory and seek a kind of equilibrium. It puts them a bit on the backfoot against the Pure as they have Luna's wrath against them but know Albretch did the righ(ish) thing. It helps that many other totems back them as well including Phoenix. They also have tentative decent relations with many Fera.<br /> <br /> So 16 (14 when I ran it), the Garou are pretty firmly divided and the next generation of Garou are starting to pop up who have only ever known this conflict between the two camps. Ironically, the Wyrm conflict has taken something of a backseat as the signs of the apocalypse are, for the moment, gone. A small group of Garou insist that this is false confidence and believe the Apocalypse was delayed rather than averted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T16:09:57-08:00","id":1438191,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I get Werewolf and Mage aren't about being human, but just like the Umbra being an option instead of a blocked off path, I think a mechanic or system of morality is important in pratically all WoD games. I'm not saying a &quot;be good&quot; morality exactly, but something akin to the Convictions (which, is whatever the hell you characters believe), and Tenets (which are &quot;these are heavy stuffs in this chronicle in particular&quot; and cause Stains), and for Werewolf, where each tribe is more social than anything, sticking to personal interpretations of a pool of belief is something that would fit WtA5 very well in my opinion. I mean, if you want, in V5, you can just ignore Touchstones, sticking with only one Conviction and put a real pulp-action Tenet selection (or simply the Litany... wherever it breeds, right?).<br /> I don't think the CoD morality, or even the old Vampire Humanity, is very fun or easy to use, but I like such things much better than &quot;ah do what you want, actions do not take toll on your conscience&quot;. Hubris works wonders for Mages. But it's also my peeve with Werewolf the Apocalypse till now, it feels a bit too much inhumane, too fictional for a game that should feel like a dark and believable reflection of our world. the interactions with fiction feel much less tangible (and less amazing) when not even my character feels human and real. But this is much more a personal than a general stroke of critique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T18:29:10-08:00","id":1438210,"title":"","content":"The hardest part of such mechanics for WtA is simple: Breeds.<br /> <br /> While all Garou have the same mental and moral capacity once they've undergone the First Change, their formative years are radically different. There are things lupus grow up thinking is perfectly normal and natural, that would strain a homid's cultural upbringing's norms, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> Forsaken made all werewolves humans, and that made designing these sorts of things much easier.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure most WtA fans (whatever they feel about Forsaken, and including myself as a big fan of Forsaken) don't want WtA to lose non-homid Breeds just to make a more satisfying &quot;emotional consequences for your actions,&quot; mechanic. But it's the kind of thing V5 taking things from VtR 2e makes people worry about (hence this thread).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T19:05:05-08:00","id":1438213,"title":"","content":"Absolutely not. If shapeshifters don't need animals then the entire game has completely different themes and is no longer Werewolf: the Apocalypse at all. It also means Red Talons, Rokea, Mokole, and a bunch of other groups never existed (and we can't play them) and the entire history of the setting from the Triassic on will be extremely retconned. As soon as the past is retconned away and rewritten from scratch, it's not the same game and loses all value for someone like me, who's invested in or playing the setting already written.<br /> <br /> It's also important to remember that other Changing-Breeds have very different psychology from Garou, and no shapeshifters have human psychology. Many years before their First Change, homids are incapable of fitting into human society because they're fundamentally inhuman. Same with lupus in wolf society. They're not supposed to feel human - that's just not the point of the game. So any morality system that's built into the mechanics like Humanity and impossible to ignore, or which wastes a bunch of ST time removing, or wastes significant page count, is something that only homid Garou can ever use and every other character type is just incompatible or unplayable.<br /> <br /> Banu Saulot, I think that maybe your experiences relate to your ST failing to use the &quot;morality&quot; mechanics Werewolf already has. Wyrm taint, Thrall of the Wyrm, falling, spiritual decay, the anger of the spirits, and the renown penalties and punishment rites for breaking the Litany are already built into the game. Every tribe already has their own particular interpretation of the Litany, and every kind of Fera has their own, different Litany and renown system. But these things aren't simple numbers to plug into a formula, and they aren't one size fits all PCs. They require effort and roleplaying and storytelling instead of just looking up a number on a table. I could understand wanting a simplified version as an alternative option, but it's just not true that Werewolf lacks morality or consequences to PC actions, from the deeply personal and spiritual to the vastly cosmic. Werewolf is a game all about consequences of human and shapeshifter behavior both past and present, just like Mage is (or can be) a game about consequencs of Mage and sleeper behavior past and present. They are also games about making hard choices without good options. If your PCs never experience consequences for anything, then your ST isn't running Werewolf as written.<br /> <br /> To be sure, Werewolf's morality mechanics and consequences are optional - not that the game is modular or balanced around ignoring them, but that the mechanics of the game aren't built to depend utterly on them. I get the impression Vampire rules would collapse without a Humanity/Path number on every character sheet, but the Werewolf rules won't collapse if you change the consequences of behavior. You don't even really need renown, you can just use the Nagah method for gaining rank. That said, the morality mechanics and consequences are in the game and ignoring them is a ST choice, not a failing of the books.<br /> <br /> <br /> The themes of being something both human and wild animal, and yet neither, and the theme of severe consequences for everyone's actions, are quite fundamental to Werewolf. I wish I could trust Paradox to hire writers who understand and value the themes of Werewolf, but what they did to Changing Ways demonstrated an overt hostility to the fundamental themes of this game that I can't ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-05-2021, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T19:21:07-08:00","id":1438216,"title":"","content":"There's a general circumstance given for characters to experience a higher temporary Rage than their normal rating that could use more fleshing out. That's probably about it on what might need to change. There's already a stat that determines reactions to stress (Rage), and a stat that measures how comfortable a character is as a shapeshifter (Primal-Urge). The former has some pretty wild fluctuations in temporary points, while the latter is only going to be low if a character purposefully tamps down on doing things the werebeast way and still goes in for human solutions (nicely demonstrated by... not putting any effort into improving it and going for, say, Craft, Technology, Drive, and Firearms instead).<br /> <br /> Note that just because their psychology isn't quite human doesn't mean that they can't feel like realized characters. They're still more relatable to living beings than undead by virtue of still having a number of frailities of life - though they get sick, poisoned or the like less often, it can still happen, and some sources of injury make the battle scars that result far, far worse than getting into a brawl with knives, cars, or falling buildings. Even the Rokea, who are by default ageless, still feel the ups and downs of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T19:31:03-08:00","id":1438222,"title":"","content":"Shapeshifters vary in how much xenofiction they are. Spider-born Ananasi are extremely inhuman, with no human experiences and no real emotions. Homid Nuwisha are fairly close to human, having Gnosis and wild animal instincts but no Rage. In between are a wide variety of character options with varying degrees of human emotions and values. They can all be complex, fully-3D characters - even the almost-completely emotionless Ananasi. But any xenofiction is more difficult than playing your own species, culture, gender, and sexual orientation.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do think it would be interesting and cool to have more details about Gnosis. It's a soul-deep connection to Gaia, fundamentally <b>knowing</b> and constantly <b>feeling</b> her love and pain and the fact that she's their mother. This has got to be a strong influence on emotions, on morals, on gut reactions, on instincts... it's the basis of their religions, the proof of their reasons to exist, <b>the</b> meaning of shapeshifter life. Yet, although there are many words written about the haze of Rage, I don't know of a book that delves into how Gnosis makes shapeshifters feel. I can only think of the mechanics for Ratkin who get too much Gnosis all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-05-2021, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:08:00-08:00","id":1438227,"title":"","content":"IMO W5 could have just a Corebook, Umbra, Changing Breeds, Triat and a Player's Guide containing a mix of Rage Across the World and Tribes, but I know that in the name of the profit they would make more books if all goes well, that would be cool. I really don't think WTA needs more meta-plot with each new edition, just updating the game chronologically and mechanically with some new options for characters. In my chronicle I put the Revised Edition-like events (like the appearing of the Eye of the Wyrm) at the &quot;endgame&quot;, my players have already some experience in WTA, so a good part of the tension is when I will say: ehh... guys... you notice a red star when you awake from your meditation.<br /> <br /> I just hope that W5 doesn't end up a reskinned WTF. I don't know if WTF 2e sold more than W20, but if it did that could signal to the company to copy and paste in the name of practicality and money. I like the animism in WTA way more than the one present in WTF, it would be a no-go for me. But, in fact, I houserule almost all the combat mechanics to be like the COD ones. There are good things to be learned from WTF, but please don't take WTA away from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:17:11-08:00","id":1438229,"title":"","content":"Why would they want to copy and paste WTF when they can just... publish more WTF? Did they not buy the rights to WTF and they did want to publish it? So why not buy the rights to it? It doesn't even make sense. But V5 doesn't make sense either.<br /> <br /> We know by now that the existence of CoD does not somehow prevent the WoD from continuing. People can buy and play both and some probably do. So what could possibly be the reason for wanting to merge them? I just don't understand it. I mean, I doubt V5 satisfies VTR fans anymore than it satisfies VTM fans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway... homid werewolves can certainly feel like they've lost their &quot;humanity&quot; and struggle to hold onto it. And an outside perspective might see that as no different from the way a vampire struggles to accept their new condition. But for a shapeshifter, this is delusion - their condition isn't new (unless they're a Skin-Dancer, but in that case they wanted to become a werewolf).<br /> <br /> On some level, even unconsciously, the First Change is a relief. It's a release of tension. It's also finally, finally, finding a place they belong. All shapehifters grow up not belonging, and not being accepted, even those born from two shapeshifters. (Except the Shinju.) All of them spend their childhood in a society that tells them their urges and thoughts and feelings are unnatural or wrong, or can't relate to or even comprehend those feelings, or tells them their body and soul are wrong (depending on breed). And then, after the Change, they finally fit in. They finally know why they were different, what those feelings meant and have a society where those feelings are accepted and acceptable. To make sense and meaning out of what was incomprehensible before, to have a language to express what was indescribable before, to have peers who <b>understand</b>. That is absolutely priceless, especially for such social creatures as werewolves (and some Fera). It is the closing of a wound they could never name or see clearly before.<br /> <br /> Fitting into this society does require giving up many of the beliefs, behaviors, and even values a homid learned from modern capitalist, monotheistic, anti-Gaian human society. And that's absolutely a struggle. Shapeshifters seem to cling to and identify personally with their beliefs in the same way humans do, and could be devastated by having their belief system undermined. But for a shapeshifter, it's a struggle to put on a shoe that truly fits, not to squeeze into a hostile society of undead puppet-masters and ruthless vampire politics that wants to eat what's left of their soul (sometimes literally).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-05-2021, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T21:37:42-08:00","id":1438248,"title":"","content":"To be a bit less hyperbolic about this, as there's pretty much zero odds W5 is going to just be WtF 2e with a thin coat of WtA paint on it:<br /> <br /> The problem is that the CofD did a lot of strong design work in the same basic space as the WoD. The 20th books are great, but they're, design-wise, still games from the 90s. There's a massive gap in time spent in new editions that overhaul some seriously outdated mechanics. So there's a natural inclination to want to look to the CofD for ideas of mechanics that can help the WoD 5e books update things to a 2020s era game line.<br /> <br /> By itself, that's not even a bad thing. I would love to see WtA have a different power systems than the current sprawling mess that is Gifts, without retreading Disciplines either. The CofD has a bunch of different models for powers at this point to look at and see if they might be better than the Gift grab-bag. Wtf 2e's Totem building system is a lot more useful than WtA's big list of Totems. Etc.<br /> <br /> The issue is that V5 didn't implement these sorts of mechanical inspirations well. They frequently feel very obviously tacked onto the game, and haven't been fine tuned to support V5's themes as well as they could have been. As such, W5 looking at mechanical inspirations elsewhere feels concerning because of that lack of attention to integration. Wtf 2e's Harmony systems are fun (to me at least), but they're not the right fit for WtA. If W5 just snags Harmony with a few tweaks, I think it would be a disservice to Harmony and to WtA. Even a better fight for WtA like CtL 2e's Clarity needs some serious work to make sure it's highlighting WtA's themes or it's not worth it.<br /> <br /> Until we have a better picture of how W5 is going to shape up, these concerns are going to linger. Though even as a fellow pessimist about it, I would caution people to not let it fester. W5 might be a good game, even if ti's going to have a lot of us saying, &quot;this isn't WtA to me, I'm sticking to W20,&quot; and there's no need to take it farther than that until we have more solid info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T21:53:07-08:00","id":1438251,"title":"","content":"Is W5 still happening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T23:14:31-08:00","id":1438269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1438251#post1438251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is W5 still happening?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apparently, but as Paradox doesn't really communicate like a normal company its hard to find the info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T16:14:16-08:00","id":1438385,"title":"","content":"I think each day I like WtA less personally. The problem is what I think would make it better in W5 for me seems to go against what the real fans of WtA like or at least would like in W5, so it's a good thing I ain't the designer or writer for it lol<br /> But I'm really interested to see how they will deal with W5, cuz, as <i>Heavy Arms </i>touched upon, the 4th editions (20th anniversary) of WoD still felt like 90s games. But although at first I had some small gripes with V5, I've grown to enjoy it by a lot. Now, more than most media, RPG permits us to make &quot;canon&quot; whatever we want in our table, so I'm happy with whatever W5 throw at us, be it system, cosmology or plot. But also hope that as many people as possible can enjoy and be satisfied by W5, that it fits their tastes and wants, etc.<br /> <br /> But I guess the thread is more about the cosmology and plot instead of mechanics right? It seems most people agree that the system could do well with an improvement and update, whatever it may be. Although I wonder if combat will stay the same as V5 does, because a werewolf combat taking 3 turns sounds a bit weird (although it's just an optional rule for quickness tbh). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:47:21-07:00","id":1439936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1438385#post1438385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think each day I like WtA less personally. The problem is what I think would make it better in W5 for me seems to go against what the real fans of WtA like or at least would like in W5, so it's a good thing I ain't the designer or writer for it lol<br /> But I'm really interested to see how they will deal with W5, cuz, as <i>Heavy Arms </i>touched upon, the 4th editions (20th anniversary) of WoD still felt like 90s games. But although at first I had some small gripes with V5, I've grown to enjoy it by a lot. Now, more than most media, RPG permits us to make &amp;quot;canon&amp;quot; whatever we want in our table, so I'm happy with whatever W5 throw at us, be it system, cosmology or plot. But also hope that as many people as possible can enjoy and be satisfied by W5, that it fits their tastes and wants, etc.<br /> <br /> But I guess the thread is more about the cosmology and plot instead of mechanics right? It seems most people agree that the system could do well with an improvement and update, whatever it may be. Although I wonder if combat will stay the same as V5 does, because a werewolf combat taking 3 turns sounds a bit weird (although it's just an optional rule for quickness tbh). </div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m the inverse. Ive been loving apocalypse more lately. Mechanically I suspect they\u2019ll utilize the same combat mechanics as v5. With their \u201cone world of darkness\u201d tag, I don\u2019t suspect they\u2019ll be changing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T17:29:23-07:00","id":1439946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1438269#post1438269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Apparently, but as Paradox doesn't really communicate like a normal company its hard to find the info.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Given that the equivalent of the JHD is being written it looks like W5 is definately in the pipeline.. but has been significantly delayed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T16:04:02-07:00","id":1440123,"title":"","content":"I suspected W5 would arrive in 2021. With the Werewolf products (two PC/Console games) making a bit of a hype buildup. I'm excited to see it either way, but WoD does best when it is given time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T17:27:37-07:00","id":1440129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1439936#post1439936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m the inverse. Ive been loving apocalypse more lately. Mechanically I suspect they\u2019ll utilize the same combat mechanics as v5. With their \u201cone world of darkness\u201d tag, I don\u2019t suspect they\u2019ll be changing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has the potential to be a terrible fit. W:tA prefers a level of splatter that would probably upset V:tM players something fierce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T22:39:25-07:00","id":1453246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1438093#post1438093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>My Werewolf: The Forsaken/Apocalypse Campaign</b><br /> <br /> Essentially the idea was that the Apocalypse was prepared and off to a good start in 2004 with the Spirit World having the Red Star as well as the Wyrm overflowing with Power. That was when King Albretch had a vision (supposedly) sent to him from Phoenix that there was a corruption in the heart of the Garou Nation that had been there for millennia. It was the source of the Wyrm being able to influence them to the Impergium, The War of Rage, and so many other horrifyingly STUPID decisions that they'd made over the years.<br /> <br /> <b>The Great Wolf</b>, a Totem that the Garou had forgotten even existed and all other Wolf Totems were a shade of like Fenris or the Old Wolf of the Woods had been corrupted by the Beast of War long ago. Albretch had a choice between either trying to redeem the Great Wolf or kill him in order to cancel the Apocalypse as it was his madness that was going to drive the Garou to all commit collective suicide by going into the Umbra for a thoroughly unnecessary glorious &quot;Ragnarok&quot;-style end.<br /> <br /> Evan Heals the Past (A Child of Gaia in my game after being rejected by the Wendigo for obvious damn reasons) argues the former but unsurprisingly, albeit perhaps disappointingly, Albretch heads with the Silver Pack to kill the Great Wolf in a strange vision quest. Possessed by an unknown spirit, Albretch and company kill the Great Wolf and the apocalypse is seemingly averted. The Red Star disappears and the Wyrm retreats. It also <i>pisses Luna off</i>. All Garou can feel her rage over what has been done and it's assumed by some that Albretch royally fucked up and others that he made a harsh but necessary call.<br /> <br /> Albretch being assassinated by someone is pretty much inevitable and happens but what follows is worse. The Garou Nation had actually been fracturing for centuries and this was the straw that broke the camel's back. Both agreed the Garou Nation had to change but two utterly incompatible visions for that emerged from the conflict.<br /> <br /> <b>The Pure</b>: A group consisting of mostly Get of Fenris, Silver Fangs, Red Talons, Wendigo, and stragglers from other tribes forms around a &quot;Return to our Roots&quot; ethos that believes the Garou need to undermine modern civilization, slaughter whoever disagrees with them, and keep the bloodlines pure. They also want to cull the Garou Nation of those who have lost their way by being too close to Homid society, befriending Fera, or being &quot;impure.&quot; It starts as a minority group but gradually grows as Luna seems to bless their actions as well as give them Gifts to kill other Garou, find new Garou faster, and breed truer.<br /> <br /> <b>The Forsaken</b>: The group consisting of everyone else but primarily the Children of Gaia, Shadow Lords, Bone Gnawers, Uktena, and Glass Walkers. They have a belief that the old ways were broken and they needed to adapt to the Modern World as well as cast aside the old mistakes. They would be guardians of mortals against the Wyrms and their territory and seek a kind of equilibrium. It puts them a bit on the backfoot against the Pure as they have Luna's wrath against them but know Albretch did the righ(ish) thing. It helps that many other totems back them as well including Phoenix. They also have tentative decent relations with many Fera.<br /> <br /> So 16 (14 when I ran it), the Garou are pretty firmly divided and the next generation of Garou are starting to pop up who have only ever known this conflict between the two camps. Ironically, the Wyrm conflict has taken something of a backseat as the signs of the apocalypse are, for the moment, gone. A small group of Garou insist that this is false confidence and believe the Apocalypse was delayed rather than averted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Man, can't believe I missed this. Thanks. I am curious though, what about the other changing breeds? Also, does the Spirit world start to resemble it's Forsaken counterpart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","user":"ryu238","date":". 06-23-2021, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T01:03:37-07:00","id":1453252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1408708#post1408708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can\u2019t Defeat the Wyrm unless you deal with things that feed the Wyrm. Pollution,Homelessness,domestic abuse,<br /> <br /> The Wyrm feeds those things and in turn it feeds them, amd you can\u2019t just claw your way out of the force of destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would homelessness and domestic abuse feed the Wyrm? Many animals are permanently homeless and have been for millions of years without it feeding the Wyrm. Lions have an incredible amount of domestic abuse and have had for millions of years without it feeding the Wyrm. It just sounds like the Wyrm is what is evil from a human perspective, and that doesn't fit in with the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T08:08:08-07:00","id":1453277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1453252#post1453252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would homelessness and domestic abuse feed the Wyrm? Many animals are permanently homeless and have been for millions of years without it feeding the Wyrm. Lions have an incredible amount of domestic abuse and have had for millions of years without it feeding the Wyrm. It just sounds like the Wyrm is what is evil from a human perspective, and that doesn't fit in with the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing to understand about the Wyrm is the <i>Garou </i>treat it that way. EVERYTHING evil is Wyrmish and nothing good is.<br /> <br /> You know, despite the fact Rage is explictly Wyrmish, Garou deny it is.<br /> <br /> The Garou are 90% right about the Spirit World but that 10% can really fuck them up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T08:09:59-07:00","id":1453278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1453246#post1453246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, can't believe I missed this. Thanks. I am curious though, what about the other changing breeds? Also, does the Spirit world start to resemble it's Forsaken counterpart?</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on the subject is that things aren't 100% Forsaken but a bit of a hybrid as things begin changing a lot more. The destruction of the Garou Nation and its shift toward more Sept-based politics has ripple effects throughout everything from Totems to ancient wars.<br /> <br /> I did establish that the Fera is a LOT more likely to have peaceful relations with the Forsaken Garou on an individual basis, though, even though there was some initial reprisals.<br /> <br /> Mostly because the Pure are even MORE aggressive in their past mistakes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T04:17:19-07:00","id":1455184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1453277#post1453277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, despite the fact Rage is explictly Wyrmish, Garou deny it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luna would like to have a word with you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T04:58:01-07:00","id":1455187,"title":"","content":"I heard that there was a source book, claiming (or retconning if you will) that Rage as is was corrupted when bestowed to the changing breeds (or only the garou), leading to the War of Rage and all that. But I never got an answer which book that might be in.... Apocalypse, maybe....<br /> <br /> Personally, I like, for all it's faults, the CoG TB revised's War of Rage passage. The Children of Gaia claiming that they made the conflict even longer lasting and brutal, since the CoG tried to broker peace and if failed again and again, and every one was better of, once they realised, that peace among the Fera was not needed or possible in that day and age and let it be.<br /> <br /> It works well, together with the Silver Crown novel, where Falcon stated, that the Silver Crown once needed the ability to command garou, but in this day and age, the crown shouldn't have anymore.<br /> <br /> I think it would also work well as an understanding between garou and other fera. They weren't meant to get along over the course of history. Only as humans evolved, and so the mindset of homid breed changed alliances became possible. Not withstanding the Beast Courts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T18:06:47-07:00","id":1455221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1455184#post1455184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Luna would like to have a word with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It comes from the Beast of War friend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T05:37:54-07:00","id":1455248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407565-chances-of-w5-being-forsaken-reskinned?p=1455221#post1455221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It comes from the Beast of War friend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to hear where that information is